{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":1414,"output":13000,"cacheRead":28352,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":12042,"totalTokens":42766,"cost":{"input":0.0006112015000000001,"output":0.02366,"cacheRead":0.0020640256,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.026335227099999997}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"We have playwright, likely chromium installed. We'll test.\n\nNow design implementation. Need six files. This is a big task. Need careful architecture to be functional and pass runtime.\n\nLet me design.\n\nGlobal sharing:\n- person.js: createPerson, animatePersonWalking.\n- world.js: WORLD, createWorld, bfsPath? createWorld returns bfsPath.\n- elevator_logic.js: IIFE window.ElevatorLogic.\n- elevator.js: class Elevator (top-level class) and window.Elevator = Elevator.\n- sim.js: uses globals. Since all classic scripts loaded, top-level declarations in world.js are globals accessible in sim.js? Yes via window global scope, but duplicate top-level lexical declarations across files problematic. Avoid same names. We'll use world constants etc. Be careful static checker sees project globals across files and duplicates.\n\nCoordinate: floors y = N*3.4. Person feet at y floor. Elevator car floor at current floor * FH. World floor slabs.\n\nSimplify world geometry yet fulfill layout. Need nav graphs and sit targets.\n\nI'll implement world building with helper functions:\n- Materials.\n- buildingGroup.\n- floor slabs strips.\n- walls.\n- furniture.\n- per-floor layouts.\n\nNavigation nodes structure: nodes as object map name -> {pos: Vector3, links: [names]}. BFS returns array of Vector3 positions excluding starting nearest? We'll define bfsPath(nodes, fromName, toName) returns waypoint positions from start node? Better: path includes all nodes including destination, maybe starting from first link. Agent walking can use path array. We need from arbitrary position to named wp. We'll implement bfsPath(nodes, fromName, toName) returns [positions of path nodes from fromName to toName] maybe exclude fromName. For sim, WALK_TO_WP on same floor: find nearest node to agent position then BFS. But BFS requires names. We can expose world.bfsPath and a helper nearestNode(nodes,pos). For cross-floor, actions route floor by floor via elevator.\n\nWorld.floor data: nodes per floor, sitTargets mapping wpName -> {sit: bool, facing: number, yOffset?}. desk waypoints names.\n\nNeed layout coordinates with building width 22 (x -11..11), depth 18 (z -9..9). Shaft 3x3 centered. Hall ring around shaft maybe at x ±2.8? But 3x3 shaft spans -1.5..1.5. Hall ring waypoints:\nhallS (0, z=2.8) in front, hallSE (3.0,2.8), hallE (3.0,0), hallNE (3.0,-2.8), hallN(0,-2.8), hallNW(-3,-2.8), hallW(-3,0), hallSW(-3,2.8), elevWait (0,0,3.8) linked hallS. Need avoid office doorway blocked. Fine.\n\nFloors 1-5 office:\n- Back offices z -9..-3, x partitions into four. Desks near z=-7? Office rooms with interior walls at x = -6? Let's do four offices across x: officeA x [-10,-5.5], B [-5.5,-1.5]? But shaft is center and back hallway around z=-2.8. Back offices along back wall z [-9,-4], with doors near z=-4 maybe. Four offices partition x -11..11 into widths 5.5: A [-11,-5.5], B[-5.5,0], C[0,5.5], D[5.5,11]. Desks at x centers -8.25,-2.75,2.75,8.25, z=-7.5. Doors at z=-4.2? Door nodes at (centerX, -3.8) linking hallN/hallNW etc. Need walls with doorway gaps. Simplify interior walls as partial segments. We can place vertical walls at x=-5.5,0,5.5 from z=-9 to -3.6 with door gaps maybe at z=-4.4? Hmm office doors facing hallway. Let's orient offices with doors on their front (z=-3.6) at x offset. Desks face -Z? Requirement desk monitor at back, user chair facing desk (-Z), chair backrest toward +Z, sit facing -Z = rotation.y = Math.PI? In Three.js default forward is +Z? Person nose +Z. rotation.y=Math.PI makes nose face -Z. So facing -Z -> rotation.y = PI. Desk at z=-7.5, monitor at z=-8.2 (back), chair at z=-6.3, person sits facing -Z. Door at z=-4.0. So office layout: door node centerX, -3.8; desk node centerX, -6.3. Walls vertical between offices, front wall of offices at z=-3.8? Hallway is around shaft at z -2.8, so space between -3.8 and -2.8 is corridor. Put front office wall at z=-4.0 with doorway gap around centerX ±0.6. Good.\n\nBack wall outer at z=-9. offices x. Desks and chairs. Add small side tables/plants maybe.\n\nConference front-left x[-11,-3], z[3,9]. Door near x=-3? Actually front-left quadrant. conf_door at (-3.2, 0, 5?) with hallSW link. HallSW (-3,2.8). Conference table center (-7, 6) with chairs on long sides facing each other across table. Table long axis X maybe x width 4, z depth 1.4. Chairs at z=4.8 and z=7.2, x=-8.2,-5.8. Seats facing table: north chairs at z=4.8 face +Z (rotation.y=0), south chairs z=7.2 face -Z (PI). conf_seat0..3. Door at (-3.2, 5.5) maybe; link hallSW and conf_center. Room walls: front outer wall already; left outer; right interior wall at x=-3, from z=3 to 9 with doorway gap near z=4.5? Back interior wall z=3 from x -11..-3 with maybe no gap? Use wall along z=3 with doorway gap near x=-3.8? Hmm simpler: conference room wall at x=-3 with door gap z 4.5..5.7, wall at z=3 full from -11 to -3. Door from hallway hallSW at (-3,2.8) through gap? Door at x=-3.5,z=5.1, hallway is around shaft x=-3,z=0..2.8. Access from hallSW via z? The room door on wall x=-3 opening to hallway that extends left? The hall ring around shaft only x -3..3, but door at x=-3.2 and z=5.1 is in front-left quadrant outside hall. We can place conf_door at (-2.5, 5.0) inside hall side and link hallSW (-3,2.8) directly; then conf_center (-7,6). But wall at x=-3 from z=3..9 with gap at z 4.4..5.6 allows crossing. Path from hallSW to conf_door to conf_center passes. Good.\n\nLounge front-right x[3,11], z[3,9], door wall x=3 gap. lounge_door (3.0,5.0), lounge_center (7,6), lounge_spot0..2 couch/armchairs. Link hallSE (3,2.8) to lounge_door. Chairs. Couch along right wall maybe x=9.2 facing -X (rotation.y=-PI/2? nose +Z default; facing -X -> rotation.y = -PI/2 gives nose? rotation y -90 maps +Z to -X yes). We'll set sit facing carefully.\n\nLounge: couch at (8.8,0,6), facing -X, seat spots at x=8.3 z=5.4,6.6? Maybe lounge_spot0 (8.2,5.6) facing -PI/2, spot1 (8.2,6.4), armchairs at (5.5,4.5) facing +Z? Let's set armchair seat nodes.\n\nWater cooler at (3.6,7.8) with water_cooler wp (4.3,7.8). Hall stands.\n\nCall panel near shaft at (1.8, floorY+1.4, 2.2?) facing +Z? mounted on shaft wall next to doors. Shaft walls? Need shaft visual. We'll build shaft walls maybe on each floor? Could be transparent frame. Elevator doors at z=1.5 (front face shaft). Call panel at x=2.0 z=1.55 facing +Z. elevator waiting at z=3.8.\n\nShaft opening: floor slabs strips leave 3x3 hole. Shaft extends. Add shaft side walls maybe opaque-ish dark gray at x±1.5 and z=-1.5, plus front wall except door opening? Could build shaft frame. We'll create vertical shaft walls perhaps as semi-transparent panels on sides from y0 to top, with front side segments around door. But elevator car moves through; front doors open. Keep simple: side walls at x±1.6 full height, back wall z=-1.6. Front wall z=1.6 maybe not, so car visible. Add door frame.\n\nLobby floor 0: lots of furniture. Need entrance gap in front wall z=9 centered x 0 width 3. We'll create front wall segments left/right and above gap for floors 1-5. The outer front wall floor0 panels x [-11,-1.5] and [1.5,11] full floor height; header above maybe y 2.4..3.4? Actually wall should have gap 3 wide full height maybe. Add header trim at y 2.8..3.4 but no collider. Fine.\n\nLobby nav:\noutside (0,0,12), threshold (0,0,9.35), entrance (0,0,7.4), lobby_center (0,0,5.2?) toward elevator. Wait elevator elevWait at z=3.8. lobby_center maybe (0,0,5.8) and link elevWait. Requirement lobby_center clear path. Then hallS etc. Link entrance and lobby_center directly to elevWait.\n\nLobby furniture: cafe left x[-11,-3], z[3,9]? That's front-left. counter on left wall x=-10.5 z=5..8; cafe_order (-9.2,6.8). bistro tables at (-7,4.8), (-5,7.4) with chairs. Cafe door from hallSW? Actually lobby has open cafe area; still add cafe_door (-3,6) linked hallSW. Front lounge right x[3,11], z[3,9] couch etc. back lounge z<0: two couches facing across table at x maybe 5.5 z=-6 and x 5.5 z=-3.2? Conversation pit back-left round table at (-7,-6) with four armchairs. Reception desk off side x=-3,z=6 maybe conflicts cafe. Prompt says reception x approx -3,z6, but cafe occupies left. Put reception at (-2.8, 6.8)? Hmm that's in walkway. Better reception near back-right? But requirement says tucked off side; we can put at x=7.5,z=7.8? Yet front lounge right. Let's put reception desk at (-2.6, 6.6) perhaps between cafe and elevator but it might block. Lobby center path x=0. Fine. But cafe door at x=-3 z5? Let's keep.\n\nLobby back: back lounge Z<0 with couches at x=5.5 z=-6 and x=5.5 z=-2.8 facing each other across coffee table at z=-4.4. Conversation pit back-left at (-7,-5.5). Water coolers at (-2.4,-2.5) and (2.4,-2.5) with wp. Reception at (-2.6,6.6) with reception wp (-2.6,7.8)? Hmm. Kiosk near entrance at (3.2,7.8). Generic loiter waypoints.\n\nNeed avoid agents standing in furniture, not critical. Collisions only agents.\n\nFurniture visuals with boxes/cylinders. Chairs with seats and backrests. For sitTargets, facing values. Important orientation. We can add chair backrest at +Z if person faces -Z, etc.\n\nPerson.js: create group with feet at y=0. Legs pivots at hip y~0.9, cylinder length 0.85 hanging. Torso 1.1 tall. Head. Arms pivot at shoulder y~1.6. Nose +Z. UserData leftLeg/rightLeg/leftArm/rightArm etc. Use palette random. Need color param shape perhaps {bodyColor, skinColor, legColor}. Use Group. Keep shadows maybe no. Add simple hair? Fine.\n\nSitting animation: legs rotation.x = -PI/2. Need check geometry: leg pivot at hip, cylinder hangs down -Y. rotation.x=-PI/2 rotates -Y direction to? Rotation about X: y' = y cos - z sin, z'= y sin + z cos. For vector (0,-1,0), angle -90: z' = (-1)*sin(-90)=1 => +Z. So feet forward +Z. But sitting person facing -Z (rotation.y=PI) makes feet local +Z -> world -Z, toward desk. Good. So -PI/2 correct. Arms drop -PI/4.\n\nWalking: use isWalking, walkPhase. When sitting set legs -PI/2 etc.\n\nWorld details and textures.\n\nElevator logic: implement robust.\n\nState machine details:\nconstructor opts floorCount=6 maxCapacity=4 floorHeight=3.4 speed maybe. States.\nProperties sets upCalls, downCalls, destinations (Set floors), passengers Set objects, pendingBoarders Map person->spot? Use Set plus spotOccupancy array; reserveBoardingSpot returns {index,x,y,z} based on index. pendingBoarders Map. pendingDisembark Set. spotOccupancy = [null x4]. doorTimer. state IDLE. direction 0. currentFloor 0 targetFloor 0. servedThisDoorCycle false? lastServedFloor.\n\nDoor timing constants: MIN_DOOR_OPEN_S=2.5? Given motion scaled at 120x, doors open 2.5 sim seconds = tiny. But motionDt = realDt*timeScale, so at 120x, 2.5 sim sec passes in 0.02 real sec! That's way too fast; but spec says lockstep with timeScale. Hmm walk speed * motionDt, so at 120x agents move huge per frame. Wait they define motionDt = realDt * timeScale and agent walk speed ~1.3 m/s, so at 120x they traverse 28m in 0.18 real sec. That is intended to play day in 5.5 min. Door open min 2.5 sim sec = 0.02 real sec ~ one frame. Boarding agents need walk to elevator during doors open; at 120x they can do it quickly but door timers. This can work but chaotic. We'll set MIN_DOOR_OPEN_S maybe 3.0, MAX 12, travel speed floors maybe 1.5 floors/s? The elevator needs be scaled. Since sim clock is fast, travel speed should also be scaled physically. Elevator speed in m/s maybe 3.0; at 120x it moves 360 m/s, crossing floor in 0.01 real sec. Fine, still lockstep. But waiting/boarding need more time. Agents walk 1.3 m/s scaled, so 3m walk takes 2.3 sim sec = 0.02 real sec. Door open 3 sim sec, good. Could be ~o