servedThisDoorCycle set true on door open; reset when doors fully close. During DOOR_CLOSING -> IDLE/MOVING not reopening. When state IDLE at floor 0 and destinations exists, pick destination. Good. But if in DOOR_OPEN at floor0 and pending boarders complete, tick doors closing after min; no reopen. Fine.\\n\\n2 passenger destinations outrank same-floor call: after closing, adding callUp(0) while at 0? If state DOOR_CLOSING then no reopen. If state IDLE at 0 and destinations nonempty, pick dest. Good. But target set at close already. We'll set target at close.\\n\\n3 repeated hall calls cannot starve riders: pick destination. Good.\\n\\n4 opposite direction calls wait: direction up with destinations above, down call at current/lower ignored until up work done. Good.\\n\\n5 door hold and safety cap: if pendingBoarders never completes, doors remain open beyond min until MAX then close. Implement.\\n\\n6 destination preserved: pressDestination(5), after travel arrives 5. Fine.\\n\\n7 reset clears all.\\n\\nPotential test constructs pendingBoarders by reserveBoard and complete. We expose passengers etc. Use object identities.\\n\\nState tick:\\n- IDLE: if work exists pick target; if target current floor and call/dest? open. else MOVING.\\n- MOVING: move toward target. Re-evaluate closer stops same direction while moving. Move y conceptual currentFloor as integer? We'll maintain position? Spec currentFloor integer. Simpler elevator moves floor-to-floor, with `travelProgress`; tick increments progress based on dt*speed/floorHeight; currentFloor set target on arrival. For rendering we can interpolate car y using logic's `carPosition` (float). Add `positionY` property. But adapter can use `visualFloor`? Provide `carY` in logic (in floors units). We'll implement `currentFloor` integer, `carY` float, `targetFloor`. Move speed floors/sec e.g. 2.5. On MOVING, set direction sign. Each tick, move carY toward targetFloor at speed floors/sec. When reached, currentFloor=targetFloor,