inations for current floor, open. We need avoid reopening same floor when servedThisDoorCycle. After close served reset, but hall call at same floor leftover may still exist and destination maybe cleared. If servedThisDoorCycle reset on close then leftover same-floor hall call could reopen before leaving. Spec says no full-car lobby starvation and same floor cannot reopen indefinitely while destinations exist. Since destinations exist, prioritize destination and don't choose current floor. Our pick when passengers>0 and dest>0 only considers dest; if dest all current floor? clear on open. So no current. Good. If no passengers, leftover hall call at same floor after doors close maybe should be served again? Could cause loop but capacity now available so fine. But for leftover callers after 4 boarded, car has passengers -> dest outrank. Good.\\n\\nWhen not passengers but destination current? cleared at open. Fine.\\n\\nRe-evaluate during MOVING:\\nCompute current continuous carY. For candidates in current direction ahead of carY and closer than target, include destinations and matching calls. Also if target was a hall call that got cleared? could retarget. Keep simple. If target floor no longer needed and there's another, update. Not necessary tests but implement.\\n\\nAdapter Elevator:\\nconstructor(scene, world) create logic. Build car group at y 0. Geometry. Add to scene. Car doors. Indicators, buttons, call panel updates.\\n\\nCar dimensions width 2.4, depth 2.2, height 2.7. position x0 z0, y = floor*FH. Floor group at local y 0? Car group origin at floor level. Build floor plane y=0.02, ceiling y=2.7, back wall z=-1.1, side walls x±1.2, doors front z=1.1. Doors half width 1.2, x ±0.6 closed. open positions x ±1.15? car width 2.4 half 1.2, door half width 1.2, open slides out beyond side -> x centers ±1.2? Actually each door half of width 1.2, closed centers -0.6,+0.6. Open each slides outward by ~1.05: centers -1.65,+1.65? That's outside car, fine; but maybe look