ck; attached people move with it.\\n\\nSim.js major.\\n\\nClock: object with simMinute, timeScale, tick(realDt), format. Need day wrap callback resetting agents and elevator. Could implement Clock class with onNewDay callback. Spec names. We'll define `const simClock = {...}` or class Clock? Use `const simClock = { ... }`. Top-level unique.\\n\\nTime scale slider log spaced 1..600. Use input range 0..100 mapping value to exp. Default 120 -> index. Compute index = log(120)/log(600)*100 ~ 78. Slider display. On input set simClock.timeScale. Add pause? not required.\\n\\nAgents:\\nMAX_WORKERS=20, MAX_VISITORS=80, MAX_OCCUPANCY=100, DEFAULT_OCCUPANCY=45.\\nWorkers 20 desk assignments: 5 floors * 4 desks = 20. Good. Assign each worker homeFloor 1..5, desk A-D. deskWpName e.g. officeA_desk. deskDoorWpName officeA_door. Sit target at desk. Worker count fixed.\\n\\nVisitors no desk.\\n\\nAgent object:\\nid, role, name, group, state, plan[], currentAction, homeFloor, deskId, deskWpName, deskDoorWpName, arrivalTime, lunchTime, lunchDuration, departureTime, hasLunched, plannedMeetingTimes, targetOccupancy etc.\\nstart position maybe outside.\\n\\nAt startup build full pool. For each: createPerson random colors, group visible false until spawn. state = DISABLED? Initial state based on id < targetOccupancy? applyOccupancy sets DISABLED if id>=targetOccupancy else AWAY. But workers id 0-19, visitors 20-99. If target 45, first 20 workers and 25 visitors enabled. Good.\\n\\nSchedule resampling per day: workers arrival 8:15-9:30, lunch etc. visitors arrival maybe now? We'll assign arrivalTime similarly but top-up overrides. departure for visitors short visit handled plan.\\n\\nSpawn: if state AWAY and clock.simMinute >= arrivalTime and within business hours maybe. Spawn at outside with jitter, visible, state ARRIVING, assign planVisitorVisit or planArriveToDesk. Need guard for workers if arrival time passed late (e.g., day starts 7:30; after wrap arrivals at 8:15; fine). If top-up sets arrivalTime now+0..6. Spawn group at outside. Ensure group added to scene if not. If was GONE removed from scene; add again.\\n\\nWe need agents not spawn after departure time perhaps. Workers: if simMinute > departureTime and AWAY -> skip until next day. For visitor top-up only during business hours (8:00-18:00 maybe). For visitors AWAY/GONE with arrivalTime <= now and now < 17:30 spawn. Top-up re-arms.\\n\\ncountPresent: states not AWAY/DISABLED/GONE.\\n\\ntopUpVisitors: during business hours 8:00..18:00 maybe 7:45..18:00; deficit = targetOccupancy - countPresent(); for visitors state AWAY/GONE and not currently enabled? If disabled skip. Re-arm arrivalTime = now + random 0..6, visitDuration, state AWAY, group invisible/removed if GONE. Only if deficit>0. Break after deficit. But if all visitors already present, no. Need not rearm visitors that are currently GONE if departure? We do.\\n\\nPotential issue: targetOccupancy 45, workers 20. Visitors arrive over time. topUp constantly re-arms GONE visitors with arrival now+0..6, so if they leave quickly, they'll come back. Good.\\n\\nVisitor plan: weighted activity, then exit. Need ensure one plan leads to exit. planVisitorVisit returns actions to walk in then activity then exit. For meetings reserve conf seat. Need choose meeting floor and seat; use world floors sitTargets. We can make helper availableSeats.\\n\\nSeat reservations global Set `seatReservations`. key floor:wp. For desk seats too? Requirement seatReservations for conf seats. Workers have own desks, no need reserve maybe but do for desk to avoid double? Each worker unique desk so fine. Visitors conference seats reserved. Lounge seats maybe too? To avoid two agents same sit spot, reserve all sit targets via seatReservations. But workers returning to desk need reserve? Could conflict if not released. Simpler: use seatReservations for all SIT spots, reserved at plan compile, released after STAND. For desk, worker's own desk always. But if a visitor sits in lounge seat, worker plan lounge may choose seat. We'll implement helper `reserveSeat(floor,wp)` returns bool, and `releaseSeat`. For worker desk plan, reserve at compile maybe; but worker might already hold reservation? At start no. We'll manage.\\n\\nHowever seatReservations persist if plan aborted (departure override). On end-of-day override release all agent's reserved seats? Track agent.reservedSeats array. releaseAgentSeats.\\n\\nSeat orientation: sitTargets[wp] = {sit:true, facing: number}. For standing targets {sit:false, facing: 0}. SIT applies facing. Need define all sit nodes.\\n\\nPlan compilers:\\n\\nActions are plain objects {type, floor, wp, dir, toFloor, minutes, state, seatKey?}. WAIT_SIM resolve at startAction: action.untilMin = simClock.simMinute + minutes (if undefined). Important if same action object reused? Plans new each time. startAction set action._started, untilMin. We'll set.\\n\\nPICK_NEXT_ACTIVITY zero duration; calls chooseNextActivity(agent) and replaces plan. We'll handle in action dispatch: after current action done, if plan empty -> chooseNextActivity. Actually plan compilers append WAIT_SIM + PICK_NEXT_ACTIVITY. PICK_NEXT_ACTIVITY itself calls choose and sets plan, then loop continues.\\n\\nState mapping: ENTER_STATE sets agent.state.\\n\\nWALK_TO_WP: Need route across floors? We'll use within current floor only; plan compilers sequence elevator rides. To walk to waypoint: agent has `floor` property (current floor). If floor mismatch maybe set? We'll assume. Use world.floors[floor].nodes, sitTargets. Find start nearest node, BFS to wp. Build path vector list from start node (or agent pos) to target. We can skip path if same. We'll set agent.path = array of {x,z,y?} positions and agent.pathIndex=0. WALK action active until path exhausted. Use world.bfsPath(nodes,startName,wp). We need nearest node to position. Implement world.nearestNode(nodes,pos). If no path, teleport? fallback direct vector.\\n\\nBFS nodes structure: We'll make each node {pos: THREE.Vector3, links: []}. For start nearest maybe could pick a node not connected due walls? all connected.\\n\\nAgent walking:\\nIn update WALK_TO_WP: if !action._started startAction sets path and currentAction data. Then each frame move toward path waypoint at speed 1.35*motionDt? Wait motionDt = realDt*timeScale, so use motionDt as simulated seconds. Speed 1.35 m/s. At 120x huge per frame. We should cap movement per frame? Spec says don't clamp below timeScale; lockstep. But huge movement may overshoot, use step = min(dist, speed*dt) and if step>=dist advance. At high dt can traverse multiple waypoints in one frame; use loop up to maybe 20 waypoints. Fine.\\n\\nStall detection: track _prevWp and _stallT using motionDt. If progress < 0.005 for >1.2 then skip waypoint. But with collision pushes progress maybe. We'll implement.\\n\\nEntrance chain exemption: while WALK_TO_WP near front door, skip collisions for agent if target wp in entrance chain or agent._entranceExempt. Set when plan includes. Simpler: collision skip if agent.currentAction.type==='WALK_TO_WP' and ['outside','front_door_threshold','entrance','lobby_center'].includes(wp). This could exempt lobby center too but okay. Also stall recovery: if near threshold and no progress >1.5 motion sec advance path index (teleport next?). Implement in walk function: if stalled near z>8.5 then set group pos to threshold/next.\\n\\nWAIT_AT_PANEL: On start: agent.state='WAITING_ELEVATOR', call elevator.callUp/Down(floor), set action._callDir, _toFloor. Each frame re-press if needed. Need only if not already accepted. Press call if not present. Then check elevator.isAcceptingAt(floor,dir) && capacityFree>0. If yes complete action -> next ENTER. If car full, wait. Also if car arrives but direction mismatch, wait. We must ensure direction for toFloor: dir = toFloor>floor ? +1:-1. Call accordingly.\\n\\nENTER_ELEVATOR(toFloor): phases reserve, walk door, board, press? We'll implement state machine within action:\\n- phase 'reserve': if no spot, if elevator.isAcceptingAt(floor,dir) && capacityFree>0 -> reserveBoardingSpot(agent); if null wait and re-press call. If car no longer accepting (left), reset reservation? If reserved but car left? Could happen if car closed doors while pending boarder? Logic holds doors for pending. So okay. Once spot, phase 'door'. Compute door threshold world pos: x = spot.x (car local x) perhaps world x same; z = 1.7 (front of car) plus maybe car current y. We need walk into door. Agent floor current. Target world (spot.x, floor*FH, 2.0?) Actually car doors at z=1.1; elevWait z=3.8. Walk to z=1.3 at x spot.x. Use direct walk with collision exemption. Move. When within 0.35 or stalled -> phase 'inside': elevator.carGroup.attach(agent.group); then set target local spot. Need preserve. After attach, group world position remains; then move to local target (spot.x, 0, spot.z) in car group local. Use local movement. Once close -> completeBoard(agent); pressDestination(toFloor); agent.floor=toFloor? Not until exit? For state maybe. Set agent.state='IN_CAR'. Then next action PRESS_FLOOR. Actually plan includes ENTER then PRESS_FLOOR then WAIT_FOR_FLOOR. We can complete ENTER after completeBoard and turn to face doors rotation.y=0. Then PRESS_FLOOR zero duration calls elevator.pressDestination(toFloor) and maybe press. Good.\\n- Need currentAction.type stays ENTER_ELEVATOR; collision exemption for all phases until complete.\\n\\nPotential doors close on pending before board? Logic holds until completeBoard. Good.\\n\\nIf car leaves before reserve? re-press call. If reserved but car leaves? Logic pending holds. Fine.\\n\\nAt high dt, local movement to spot immediate.\\n\\nPRESS_FLOOR: pressDestination(floor) where floor=action.floor (toFloor); complete immediately.\\nWAIT_FOR_FLOOR: each frame if elevator.state==='DOOR_OPEN' && currentFloor===floor then complete. Also if not in car? Fine.\\nEXIT_ELEVATOR(toFloor): on start: registerDisembark(agent); maybe phase 'walkout': target local position (spot.x maybe, 0, 1.8) then scene.attach when beyond doors? Simpler: immediately scene.attach(group) preserving world pos, set y=floor*FH, then walk to elevWait with collision exempt. But if doors open, step out. Requirement reparent preserving world pos and walk to elevWait; completeDisembark. Do:\\n- start: elevator.registerDisembark(agent); scene.attach(group); group.position.y = floor*FH; agent.floor=floor; agent.state='ON_FLOOR'; set path direct to elevWait? Actually position inside car z~±0.6. Need move out to z=3.8. Use direct target. Each frame move; when close, completeDisembark(agent); complete action. registerDisembark holds doors while exiting. If we completeDisembark after reaching elevWait, doors held long enough. Collision exemption for EXIT_ELEVATOR.\\n\\nBut scene.attach then position y=floor*FH resets to car floor same. Good. However car may move immediately after doors close while agent still exiting; pendingDisembark holds doors until complete. Good.\\n\\nSIT(floor,wp): on start find target world pos (node pos). Snap x,z, set y=floor*FH - 0.35. apply rotation.y=facing. isSitting=true. state maybe set by ENTER_STATE before. Reserve seat at plan compile. For standing target jitter. For sit target maybe snap exactly. Note node position is seat center. Set group y. Complete immediately.\\nSTAND: isSitting=false; y = agent.floor*FH (or if in car? car local y 0; agent.floor? use parent car). We set group.position.y=0 if parent is car else floor*FH. state maybe.\\nRELEASE_SEAT: release action.seatKey or agent's; complete.\\n\\nWAIT_SIM: start sets untilMin = simClock.simMinute + minutes. If minutes undefined maybe use random. Wait until simMinute >= untilMin. Complete. At high timescale fine.\\nEXIT_BUILDING: remove group from scene, state GONE, visible false, complete plan done. For workers GONE until next day; visitors top-up re-arms. Also release seats.\\n\\nENTER_STATE(state): set agent.state; complet