vedThisDoorCycle set true on door open; reset when doors fully close. During DOOR_CLOSING -> IDLE/MOVING not reopening. When state IDLE at floor 0 and destinations exists, pick destination. Good. But if in DOOR_OPEN at floor0 and pending boarders complete, tick doors closing after min; no reopen. Fine.\\n\\n2 passenger destinations outrank same-floor call: after closing, adding callUp(0) while at 0? If state DOOR_CLOSING then no reopen. If state IDLE at 0 and destinations nonempty, pick dest. Good. But target set at close already. We'll set target at close.\\n\\n3 repeated hall calls cannot starve riders: pick destination. Good.\\n\\n4 opposite direction calls wait: direction up with destinations above, down call at current/lower ignored until up work done. Good.\\n\\n5 door hold and safety cap: if pendingBoarders never completes, doors remain open beyond min until MAX then close. Implement.\\n\\n6 destination preserved: pressDestination(5), after travel arrives 5. Fine.\\n\\n7 reset clears all.\\n\\nPotential test constructs pendingBoarders by reserveBoard and complete. We expose passengers etc. Use object identities.\\n\\nState tick:\\n- IDLE: if work exists pick target; if target current floor and call/dest? open. else MOVING.\\n- MOVING: move toward target. Re-evaluate closer stops same direction while moving. Move y conceptual currentFloor as integer? We'll maintain position? Spec currentFloor integer. Simpler elevator moves floor-to-floor, with `travelProgress`; tick increments progress based on dt*speed/floorHeight; currentFloor set target on arrival. For rendering we can interpolate car y using logic's `carPosition` (float). Add `positionY` property. But adapter can use `visualFloor`? Provide `carY` in logic (in floors units). We'll implement `currentFloor` integer, `carY` float, `targetFloor`. Move speed floors/sec e.g. 2.5. On MOVING, set direction sign. Each tick, move carY toward targetFloor at speed floors/sec. When reached, currentFloor=targetFloor, state=DOOR_OPENING. But re-evaluate target while moving: choose closer stop same direction; if target changes and it is behind? only ahead. Could just set target if closer than current target and ahead of current position. Fine.\\n\\nDoor states:\\nDOOR_OPENING: doorTimer += dt; if >= doorOpenTime (1.2) -> DOOR_OPEN, doorTimer=0, onOpen(floor): clear destination at floor, clear served hall call direction. Also clear opposite if no remaining stops in direction. servedThisDoorCycle=true, lastServedFloor=floor. Need set direction based on hall call if idle? On arrival direction already set. If direction 0 and call at floor, infer from calls. But pick target infers.\\n\\nDOOR_OPEN: doorTimer += dt. if pending sets empty and doorTimer>=MIN -> state DOOR_CLOSING, doorTimer=0. If >=MAX -> force close (and maybe clear pending? no, but close). On force close, pending might remain; need clear? If never completes, test expects close. Keep pending maybe but reset? To avoid jam, clear pending boarders and release spots? Probably clear pending boarders. But test may assert state. We'll clear pendingBoarders and pendingDisembark and release spots on forced close? Not specified; but safety. We can do clear pending and spot occupancy for pending entries.\\n\\nDOOR_CLOSING: doorTimer; after doorCloseTime (1.0) -> doors closed; state IDLE; servedThisDoorCycle=false; pick target immediately maybe state MOVING. If no work IDLE direction 0 target current floor.\\n\\nCall clearing at open:\\n- if direction +1 clear upCalls floor; also destinations delete floor.\\n- if direction -1 clear downCalls.\\n- if direction 0 clear both calls? If car idle at floor and opens due call, direction inferred.\\n- If after clearing no stops ahead in current direction, clear opposite call at this floor too.\\n\\nisAcceptingAt(floor,direction): state DOOR_OPEN && currentFloor===floor && (no more stops pending in current direction || dir matches car direction). More precisely: hasStopsAhead(direction) false OR