lounge seat, worker plan lounge may choose seat. We'll implement helper `reserveSeat(floor,wp)` returns bool, and `releaseSeat`. For worker desk plan, reserve at compile maybe; but worker might already hold reservation? At start no. We'll manage.\\n\\nHowever seatReservations persist if plan aborted (departure override). On end-of-day override release all agent's reserved seats? Track agent.reservedSeats array. releaseAgentSeats.\\n\\nSeat orientation: sitTargets[wp] = {sit:true, facing: number}. For standing targets {sit:false, facing: 0}. SIT applies facing. Need define all sit nodes.\\n\\nPlan compilers:\\n\\nActions are plain objects {type, floor, wp, dir, toFloor, minutes, state, seatKey?}. WAIT_SIM resolve at startAction: action.untilMin = simClock.simMinute + minutes (if undefined). Important if same action object reused? Plans new each time. startAction set action._started, untilMin. We'll set.\\n\\nPICK_NEXT_ACTIVITY zero duration; calls chooseNextActivity(agent) and replaces plan. We'll handle in action dispatch: after current action done, if plan empty -> chooseNextActivity. Actually plan compilers append WAIT_SIM + PICK_NEXT_ACTIVITY. PICK_NEXT_ACTIVITY itself calls choose and sets plan, then loop continues.\\n\\nState mapping: ENTER_STATE sets agent.state.\\n\\nWALK_TO_WP: Need route across floors? We'll use within current floor only; plan compilers sequence elevator rides. To walk to waypoint: agent has `floor` property (current floor). If floor mismatch maybe set? We'll assume. Use world.floors[floor].nodes, sitTargets. Find start nearest node, BFS to wp. Build path vector list from start node (or agent pos) to target. We can skip path if same. We'll set agent.path = array of {x,z,y?} positions and agent.pathIndex=0. WALK action active until path exhausted. Use world.bfsPath(nodes,startName,wp). We need nearest node to position. Implement world.nearestNode(nodes,pos). If no path, teleport? fallback direct vector.\\n\\nBFS nodes structure: We'll make each node {pos: THREE.Vector3, links: []}. For start nearest maybe could pick a node not connected due walls? all connected.\\n\\nAgent walking:\\nIn update WALK_TO_WP: if !action._started startAction sets path and currentAction data. Then each frame move toward path waypoint at speed 1.35*motionDt? Wait motionDt = realDt*timeScale, so use motionDt as simulated seconds. Speed 1.35 m/s. At 120x huge per frame. We should cap movement per frame? Spec says don't clamp below timeScale; lockstep. But huge movement may overshoot, use step = min(dist, speed*dt) and if step>=dist advance. At high dt can traverse multiple waypoints in one frame; use loop up to maybe 20 waypoints. Fine.\\n\\nStall detection: track _prevWp and _stallT using motionDt. If progress < 0.005 for >1.2 then skip waypoint. But with collision pushes progress maybe. We'll implement.\\n\\nEntrance chain exemption: while WALK_TO_WP near front door, skip collisions for agent if target wp in entrance chain or agent._entranceExempt. Set when plan includes. Simpler: collision skip if agent.currentAction.type==='WALK_TO_WP' and ['outside','front_door_threshold','entrance','lobby_center'].includes(wp). This could exempt lobby center too but okay. Also stall recovery: if near threshold and no progress >1.5 motion sec advance path index (teleport next?). Implement in walk function: if stalled near z>8.5 then set group pos to threshold/next.\\n\\nWAIT_AT_PANEL: On start: agent.state='WAITING_ELEVATOR', call elevator.callUp/Down(floor), set action._callDir, _toFloor. Each frame re-press if needed. Need only if not already accepted. Press call if not present. Then check elevator.isAcceptingAt(floor,dir) && capacityFree>0. If yes complete action -> next ENTER. If car full, wait. Also if car arrives but direction mismatch, wait. We must ensure direction for toFloor: dir = toFloor>floor ? +1:-1. Call accordingly.\\n\\nENTER_ELEVATOR(toFloor): phases reserve, walk door, board, press? We'll implement state machine within action:\\n- phase 'reserve': if no spot, if elevator.isAcceptingAt(floor,dir) && capacityFree>0 -> reserveBoardingSpot(agent); if null wait and re-press call. If car no longer accepting (left), reset reservation? If reserved but car left? Could happen if car closed doors while pending boarder? Logic holds doors for pending. So okay. Once spot, phase 'door'. Compute door threshold world pos: x = spot.x (car local x) perhaps world x same; z = 1.7 (front of car) plus maybe car current y. We need walk into door. Agent floor current. Target world (spot.x, floor*FH, 2.0?) Actually car doors at z=1.1; elevWait z=3.8. Walk to z=1.3 at x spot.x. Use direct walk with collision exemption. Move. When within 0.35 or stalled -> phase 'inside': elevator.carGroup.attach(agent.group); then set target local spot. Need preserve. After attach, group world position remains; then move to local target (spot.x, 0, spot.z) in car group local. Use local movement. Once close -> completeBoard(agent); pressDestination(toFloor); agent.floor=toFloor? Not until exit? For state maybe. Set agent.state='IN_CAR'. Then next action PRESS_FLOOR. Actually plan includes ENTER then PRESS_FLOOR then WAIT_FOR_FLOOR. We can complete ENTER after completeBoard and turn to face doors rotation.y=0. Then PRESS_FLOOR zero duration calls elevator.pressDestination(toFloor) and maybe press. Good.\\n- Need currentAction.type stays ENTER_ELEVATOR; collision exemption for all phases until complete.\\n\\nPotential doors close on pending before board? Logic holds until completeBoard. Good.\\n\\nIf car leaves before reserve? re-press call. If reserved but car leaves? Logic pending holds. Fine.\\n\\nAt high dt, local movement to spot immediate.\\n\\nPRESS_FLOOR: pressDestination(floor) where floor=action.floor (toFloor); complete immediately.\\nWAIT_FOR_FLOOR: each frame if elevator.state==='DOOR_OPEN' && currentFloor===floor then complete. Also if not in car? Fine.\\nEXIT_ELEVATOR(toFloor): on start: registerDisembark(agent);