cos. For +Z vector (0,0,1), y=PI/2 -> x'=1, z'=0 -> +X. yes.\n- cafe_door node (-3,6) linked hallSW. It's just waypoint.\n- Front lounge right: couch at (9.2,6) facing -X, seats maybe front_lounge0 (8.55,5.5) facing -PI/2, front_lounge1 (8.55,6.5). Armchairs at (5.3,4.4) facing toward table (7,6) angle 2.3? Add front_lounge2 (5.4,4.4) facing 2.3, front_lounge3 (5.4,7.6) facing -2.3 maybe. Coffee table (7,6).\n- Back lounge Z<0: two couches facing each other across coffee table. Couch A at x=5.5,z=-7.0 facing +Z (rotation 0), seats at (4.8,-6.4) facing +Z? Person sits at z=-6.4, couch backrest behind at z=-7.0. Couch B at x=5.5,z=-2.6 facing -Z, seats (4.8,-3.2) facing PI. Wait couches face each other across table at z=-4.8. Use back_lounge_N at (4.8,-6.3) facing 0? Table z=-4.8, person z=-6.3 faces +Z yes. back_lounge_S (4.8,-3.3) facing PI. Coffee table at (5.5,-4.8).\n  Add couch geometry for each with backrest behind.\n- Conversation pit back-left: round table (-7,-5.5) radius 1.0 at y .75. Four armchairs at pit_N (-7,-7.3) facing 0? Table at z=-5.5, chair at z=-7.3 faces +Z -> 0. pit_S (-7,-3.7) facing PI. pit_E (-5.2,-5.5) facing -PI/2 (toward -X), pit_W (-8.8,-5.5) facing PI/2 (+X). Add chairs. sitTargets.\n- Reception desk at (-2.6,6.7)? That might overlap cafe door. Let's instead put reception at (7.8,7.8) in front lounge? Hmm front-right lounge. Maybe at (-2.6,7.8) near entrance left. Prompt says approx -3,6. Put reception desk at (-3.0,7.6) with desk box 2.2x1x0.8, reception wp (-3.0,6.9) in front. Cafe door (-4.8,6.0)? Hmm cafe occupies left. The lobby center path x0. Reception at x=-3,z7.6 not blocking. But cafe bistro table at -5,7.4 near. Fine. Link reception to lobby_center.\n- Kiosk at (3.2,7.6) with kiosk wp (3.2,6.9). Plant near entrance x±2.2,z8.2.\n- Water coolers at (-2.2,-2.4) and (2.2,-2.4) with wp maybe (-2.2,-1.7) and (2.2,-1.7). But hallway ring around shaft has hallN z=-2.8, so water coolers may conflict. Put front wc at (2.4,7.0) and back