t create colliders, visual only. Use addBox with height FH-0.2.\\n\\nFloors 1..5:\\n- back office partitions: vertical walls at x=-5.5,0,5.5 from z=-9 to -4.0, height 2.6, with doorway gaps? Door in front wall z=-4.0. Use vertical partition walls full from z=-9 to -4.0, but at x=0 shaft back? Shaft z -1.5..1.5, so x=0 wall z -9..-4 fine. Office front wall z=-4.0 with segments for each office leaving center door gap 1.2. For office A x -11..-5.5, door at center x -8.25, gap x -8.85..-7.65; segments x -11..-8.85 and -7.65..-5.5. Similar.\\n- Office desks: desk box at (cx, y+0.38, -7.3), dimensions 2.0x0.12x0.9 top; legs maybe. Monitor at back z=-7.65 y+0.8. Chair at (cx, floorY, -6.1) facing -Z. Seat box .6x.12x.6 at y .45; backrest at z=-5.75? If facing -Z, backrest is +Z side (behind person) so z = -6.1 + 0.28 = -5.82, height .55. Person sits at z=-6.1. Desk front at z=-6.85? Desk center -7.3 depth .9 spans -7.75..-6.85. Person at -6.1, feet forward -Z reach -6.6 under desk maybe. Good.\\nSit target desk at (cx, floorY, -6.1), facing PI (nose -Z).\\nNode officeX_desk at same; officeX_door at (cx, floorY, -3.9)? Wall at z=-4, door gap. Put door node at (cx,0,-3.55) hallway side maybe. Link to desk. Link door to nearest hall corner: A -> hallNW (-3,-2.8)? A x -8.25; maybe link to hallNW and hallN. B -> hallN? For B center -2.75 near x0 -> hallN (0,-2.8). C -> hallN (0,-2.8) or hallNE. D -> hallNE (3,-2.8). We'll link each door to both hallN and nearest side? Simpler: officeA_door -> hallNW, officeB_door -> hallN, officeC_door -> hallN, officeD_door -> hallNE. BFS fine.\\n\\nNeed office door node maybe at (cx,-3.55) and desk at (cx,-6.1). Path crosses gap. Good.\\n\\n- Conference room: Walls at z=3 (from x -11..-3) with door gap near x=-3? Hmm door is in x=-3 wall. We'll build wall z=3 from -11..-3.8 maybe and leave corner open? Better: conference boundary: back wall z=3 from x -11..-3; right wall x=-3 from z=3..9 with doorway gap z 4.3..5.5. Add segments. Door node (-