r 0.\n- servedThisDoorCycle false, lastServedFloor -1.\n- doorCycleId? not needed.\n\nreserveBoardingSpot: if free <=0 return null; choose free index among spotCount. If passenger count can be 4. pendingBoarders size + passengers size < max. Find free spot. If none return null. spot occupancy. Return {index,x,y,z}. Spots local maybe:\n```\n[{x:-0.55,z:0.55},{x:0.55,z:0.55},{x:-0.55,z:-0.55},{x:0.55,z:-0.55}]\n```\nNeed all within car. okay.\n\ncompleteBoard: if pendingBoarders.has(person) { delete; passengers.add(person); } If called without reservation maybe add anyway? Tests may directly call? Required sequence likely reserve then complete. But robust: if no pending, if capacity free, add to passengers and assign? We'll just add and if no spot? fine. We can add. But capacity could exceed. We'll implement if pending has -> move; else if passengers.size<maxCapacity -> passengers.add.\nregisterDisembark(person) add pending.\ncompleteDisembark(person): passengers.delete; pendingDisembark.delete; release spot.\n\nReset clears all.\n\nisAcceptingAt(floor, direction):\n- if state !== DOOR_OPEN or currentFloor!==floor return false.\n- if this.direction===0 return true.\n- if direction !== this.direction return false? If no stops ahead in current direction, then accept opposite. Compute hasStopsAhead.\nSpec: true only when at floor DOOR_OPEN AND either no more stops pending in current direction OR caller's direction matches car's. So if hasStopsAhead(dir) then direction must equal. But also if caller dir is opposite while car direction up but no up work left, true. If car direction up and up work remains, a down caller at this floor should not board. Good.\nNeed hasStopsAhead(direction) includes destinations or hall calls strictly ahead in direction. If direction 0 maybe check both. Implement.\n\nPick next target at door close / idle:\n```\n_pickNextTarget() {\n const current=this.currentFloor;\n const hasDest=this.destinations.size>0;\n const candidates=[];\n dests -> {fl