s includes window.createDisplayTexture; but in elevator.js referencing createDisplayTexture global may resolve because projectGlobals includes it. Good. Could use window.createDisplayTexture explicitly to be safe.\n\nAdapter mirrors properties: we can define getters or assign in tick. sim reads elevator.state etc. We'll define getters for state/direction/currentFloor/targetFloor/upCalls/downCalls/destinations/passengers/pendingBoarders/pendingDisembark. Since getters on class maybe static checker class scope parse okay. Simpler in constructor define `this.logic=...` and in tick set `this.state=this.logic.state` etc. But sim may access before first tick? after constructor we can sync. Also methods delegate. Use getters is clean:\n```\nget state(){return this.logic.state}\n...\n```\nStatic checker class method param parse may be okay. But top-level duplicate no. We'll use getters.\n\nMethods callUp etc delegate.\n\ntick(dt): logic.tick(dt); sync visuals. Car y = logic.carY * FH. door openness. state/timer. Set doors. Update indicators. update call panels.\n- For each floor f, panel.setUp(upCalls.has(f)), setDown, setIndicator(displayText). Display text current floor plus direction arrow: if f===currentFloor then `${currentFloor}${dir>0?'^':dir<0?'v':'-'}` else maybe current floor with arrow? Requirement current floor indicator on each floor shows car current floor and direction. So same text for all. setIndicator(`${currentFloor}${arrow}`).\n- shaftIndicator same.\n- inCar indicator same text maybe.\n- buttons: material = (destinations.has(f) || (state OPEN && currentFloor===f)) ? glow : dim. Buttons store.\n- door target: based state: OPEN=>1, OPENING=>min(1,doorTimer/doorOpenTime), CLOSING=>max(0,1-doorTimer/doorCloseTime), else 0. Use lerp? At high speed direct. Set door positions x = ±(0.6 + openness*1.05), maybe z remains. Actually doors slide outward to sides; okay.\n\nNeed call panel maybe floor0 etc.\n\nCarGroup named. Expose carGroup. Also `group` maybe for s