n.phase='inside'; }\n  else { pos.x += dx/dist*step; pos.z += dz/dist*step; pos.y=floor*FH; rotation.y=atan2(dx,dz);}\n  // stall: if no progress 1.5 motion sec, teleport threshold\n  ...\n  return false;\n}\nif (action.phase==='inside') {\n  elevator.carGroup.attach(agent.group);\n  agent.state='IN_CAR';\n  action.phase='spot';\n  // after attach, group local pos should be near door\n}\nif (action.phase==='spot') {\n  const localTarget = new THREE.Vector3(action.spot.x, 0, action.spot.z);\n  const pos=agent.group.position; dx=localTarget.x-pos.x; dz=localTarget.z-pos.z; dist...\n  step=AGENT_WALK_SPEED*dt;\n  if (dist<=0.08 || step>=dist) { pos.copy(localTarget); elevator.completeBoard(agent); agent.group.rotation.y=0; return true; }\n  else move...\n  return false;\n}\n```\nNeed doors hold for pendingBoarders. We reserve then walk. Good.\nBut if car moves while boarder walking? Logic holds pending. Car stays. Good.\nIf car is not at floor (slipped away) after reservation? We check isAccepting before reserve. Could car start closing while pending? No, pending prevents closing. If max door timer force closes, pending cleared, boarder may still be walking; then car may leave. Our action phase door should re-check if state not open at floor; then release spot? There's no release method. Could call completeBoard? Hmm. Edge. We can if car leaves and phase door and not at floor, reset action.spot? But spotOccupancy stuck. Add logic method releaseBoardingSpot? Not specified. We can avoid by reservation only when open and then car holds. Safety cap 18 sim sec might force if at 600x walk takes <1 frame, so no. Fine.\n\nNeed walking collision exemption for ENTER_ELEVATOR in applyCollisions.\n\nPRESS_FLOOR: press destination action.floor; maybe set state IN_CAR. complete.\nWAIT_FOR_FLOOR: if elevator.state==='DOOR_OPEN' && currentFloor===action.floor return true. Also if state maybe door closing? no. agent state IN_CAR. Maybe if not in car? no.\nEXIT_ELEVATOR:\nstart: elevato