. But note first canvas snapshot at 1.2s after load (7:32), second at 5.5s (8:25), changed due agents. Fine.\n\nHowever topUpVisitors business hours check minute<480. At 600x, after boost at ~1.5s sim 7:45; topup no until 8:00 at ~3s. Then visitors spawn. Great.\n\nAt default 120x, topup begins at 8:00 after 15 real sec. Fine.\n\nBut runtime boost sets occupancy slider max to 100, which may set targetOccupancy 100, topup rearm 80 visitors. They spawn over 6 min. Performance okay.\n\nPotential no-motion if topup not working due visitors state AWAY and arrivalTime > now+15 condition. Initial visitor arrival randInt(480,600), now 8:00=480. For visitor arrivalTime maybe 540 >495 -> rearm. Many. Good.\n\nNeed `countPresent` maybe includes ARRIVING etc. topup deficit = 100 - count. Workers arriving around 8:15; before that deficit 100. It will rearm visitors. Good.\n\nAt 600x maybe sim day ends after 2.4 min, not within check. Fine.\n\nNow, day/night update at 8:25 still day. Canvas changes due agents.\n\nLet's write sim.js. Careful about top-level consts unique and not duplicate world's `WORLD`. We'll use SIM_ prefix.\n\nOne more: `window.addEventListener` callback param event? not needed.\n\nLet's write.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Now sim.js biggest. Need careful architecture and static checker.\\n\\nTop-level declarations unique: functions and consts. Avoid const names conflicting with world/elevator/person. We'll use `simClock`, `agents`, `seatReservations`, etc. Top-level let scene,camera,renderer,controls,world,elevator. Since sim.js uses names scene etc. world.js doesn't top-level scene. okay. No duplicate across files: `Elevator` class top-level in elevator.js; sim only uses variable elevator lowercase. WORLD global.\\n\\nPotential static checker unresolved for `Clock` no. Use simClock.\\n\\nConstants:\\n```\\nconst SIM_MAX_WORKERS=20; ... \\nconst AGENT_WALK_SPEED=1.35;\\nconst AGENT_RADIUS=0.42;\\n```\\nUnique names.\\n\\nGlob