\n17.5: 0xb97b52 sun 0xff9a55 .55 amb .48 hemi .42\\n18: 0x5c4a5e sun 0xcc7744 .3 amb .46 hemi .36\\n18.5: 0x1b2233 sun 0x7788aa .14 amb .45 hemi .32\\n24 same.\\nLong flat day. Good.\\n\\nAgent creation:\\nName arrays. Worker desks. Build full pool at startup:\\n```\\nfunction buildAgents() {\\n for i<20: role WORKER, homeFloor = Math.floor(i/4)+1, desk = world.floors[homeFloor].desks[i%4], name random, group=createPerson(), group.visible=false, state AWAY, ...\\n for v<80: role VISITOR, homeFloor=null...\\n assign ids.\\n}\\n```\\nNeed createPerson uses THREE. Called after world created. Add group to scene initially? We can add to scene and visible false. But GONE remove; on spawn re-add. Keep scene add for all initially visible false. On EXIT_BUILDING remove. On spawn if not parent scene add. If parent car? reset detach.\\n\\nAgent fields:\\n```\\n{\\n id, role, name, group, state:'AWAY', floor:0, plan:[], currentAction:null,\\n homeFloor, deskId, deskWpName, deskDoorWpName,\\n arrivalTime, lunchTime, lunchDuration, departureTime, hasLunched:false,\\n plannedMeetingTimes:[], visitDuration, reservedSeats: [], leaving:false,\\n path:[], pathIndex:0, spawn...\\n}\\n```\\ncreatePerson palettes. group.userData.agent=agent maybe.\\n\\n`resampleSchedule(agent, initial)`:\\nWorkers:\\narrivalTime = randInt(495,570) (8:15..9:30)\\nlunchTime = randInt(690,810)\\nlunchDuration = randInt(25,60)\\ndeparture = randInt(1005,1110); if Math.random()<0.15 departure=randInt(1110,1185)\\nmeetings: maybe 0,1,2. Generate morning 570..690, afternoon 810..960. 60% chance each? Spec 0..2. Use if random<0.65 add morning, <0.6 add afternoon, maybe cap.\\nhasLunched=false; leaving=false; plan=[]; currentAction=null; reservedSeats release.\\nVisitors:\\narrivalTime = initial ? randInt(480,600) : simClock.simMinute + randInt(0,6)\\nvisitDuration = randInt(30,100)\\nlunchTime etc not needed but set departureTime=arrival+duration; hasLunched true maybe; plannedMeetingTimes=[].\\nState handled by reset.\\n\\n`resetDay()`:\\n- release all seatReservations clear.\\n- for each agent: detach from car if needed? if parent !== scene maybe scene.attach? but day reset. Set group.visible false; remove from scene if parent; state DISABLED if id>=targetOccupancy else AWAY; plan=[]; currentAction=null; group.userData.isSitting=false; isWalking=false; group.position.set(0,0,12) maybe; reservedSeats=[]; leaving=false; floor=0; resample schedule. For visitors schedule arrivalTime maybe now+random? For resetDay at midnight, business hours later; set arrivalTime randInt(480,600) for workers and visitors initial? For visitors maybe randInt(480,600) but top-up will rearm. Use resampleSchedule(agent, true) for all. For workers arrival. For visitors arrival randInt(480,600).\\n- elevator.reset().\\n- seatReservations.clear().\\n\\nNeed not reinitialize roles/desks.\\n\\n`applyOccupancy()`: for each agent if id<targetOccupancy: if state DISABLED -> state AWAY; if id>= target and state in AWAY/GONE? Spec flip DISABLED<->AWAY based on id; agents mid-workday left running, will finish naturally reach GONE and only parked DISABLED next day-wrap. But slider reduction should maybe set active agents? It says \\\"Agents that are already in the middle of a workday ... are left running - they'll finish naturally, reach GONE, and only be parked DISABLED on the next day-wrap.\\\" So for agents id>=target with state AWAY -> DISABLED; GONE -> maybe leave GONE until next day? It says flip DISABLED<->AWAY based on id. But GONE? Could set DISABLED for GONE too, removing group. Active left. For id<target, DISABLED->AWAY. We'll implement:\\n```\\nif enabled && state==='DISABLED' state='AWAY';\\nif !enabled && (state==='AWAY') state='DISABLED';\\nif !enabled && state==='GONE' { state='DISABLED'; hide; }\\n```\\nBut if active id>= target leave. On next day reset uses target. Also topUp should skip disabled.\\n\\n`countPresent`: state not DISABLED/AWAY/GONE. Include ARRIVING etc.\\n\\n`topUpVisitors`