get sit, group y floorY-0.35. But person origin feet at 0 and hips .9; chair seat height .46. Lowering .35 gives hips .55, close. Good.\nFor standing jitter, y floorY.\nSet agent.state maybe already set by ENTER_STATE. For visitor desk? no.\n\n`STAND` start maybe if agent parent car? y=0. if scene y=floor*FH.\n`RELEASE_SEAT`: release key or all. return true.\n`EXIT_BUILDING`: remove. Also if agent.group.parent===elevator.carGroup? scene.attach? just remove from parent. release seats. state GONE. visible false. leaving=false. Maybe agent.floor=0. return true.\n`ENTER_STATE`: set.\n`MARK_LUNCHED`: set.\n`PICK_NEXT_ACTIVITY`: chooseNextActivity; return true.\n`WALK_TO_WP`: start builds path; process walk. Need if path empty return true? if no path, teleport maybe. We'll set path to target node if exists. If still empty return true.\n\nPath building nearest node may choose node on wrong floor? nodes per floor. fine.\n\n`walkAlongPath` should use agent.floor for y. But if path node positions have y floor*FH. We'll set pos.y = agent.floor*FH each step.\n\nStall detection with dt: At low speed dt .016, moved ~.02 > .005, so no stall. If blocked, moved maybe collision pushes <.005. after 1.2 sec skip. Good. At high dt, moved huge. Good.\n\nBut collision pushes agent, walk movement also. Fine.\n\n`isEntranceChain` includes outside threshold entrance lobby_center.\n\n`applyCollisions` skip if agent.group.parent===elevator.carGroup. Since car parent comparison. We can check `if (a.group.parent === elevator.carGroup) continue` inside loop. If both in car skip.\n\nPotential performance of updateLighting every frame with Color lerp new? Use temp colors global? We can create inside but 300 frames fine. Use `const colorA = new THREE.Color(...)` each frame maybe okay. Better keyframes store hex and use temp. Simplicity.\n\nHUD stats counts per state. Build object. Use states array. Update text only maybe each frame okay. Could throttle but fine.\n\nNeed `window.__sim...` not necessary. But runtime boost sets sliders; maybe it can't find if sliders not range? we create range.\n\nRuntime dynamic changes: agents moving and clock changes. At load time 7:30, agents arrive 8:15 so for first 1.2 sec at 120x advances 2.4 sim min to 7:32, no agents. But elevator maybe idle, lighting changes slowly, canvas may change due lighting? At 120x, sim time advances 144 sec? Wait real 1.2s *120 =144 sim seconds =2.4 min. Lighting at 7:30 flat same keyframes 7-12, no change. Canvas checksum might be identical! Then runtime after boost sets speed 600 and occupancy 100, waits 4.2s -> sim advances 42 min from 7:32 to 8:14, agents start arriving around 8:15 maybe at very end. Lighting flat. But dynamic_changes counts object position changes from patched updateMatrixWorld. If no agents move and elevator static, dynamic_changes=0 => no-motion. Need ensure motion within probe. We should spawn some early visitors/agents at start (7:30) or make elevator move? Prompt expected people starting around 8:30, but runtime check 5.5s at 600x gets to ~8:15. Could still be no motion until near end, maybe dynamic changes >0 if last frames agents spawn around 8:14. But risk.\n\nTo guarantee dynamic changes, perhaps initial schedule visitors arrival 7:35..9:00? But expected around 8:30. Could add a few \"early bird\" workers arrival 7:35..8:00. Real office has early arrivals. Or start clock 7:30 but set some workers arrival 7:35. Requirement worker arrival 8:15..9:30 though. Hmm. Runtime boost sets occupancy max and speed max, but only 5.5 sec. At 600x, 5.5s*600=3300 sim sec=55 min, from 7:30 to 8:25. So agents with arrival 8:15 will spawn in last 10 min = 0.6 real sec. Enough for dynamic changes likely. Also topUpVisitors only after 8:00. At 8:00 it re-arms visitors, arrival now+0..6, so they spawn ~8:00-8:06; that's ~0.6s before end? Actually from 7:30 to 8:00 is 30 sim min = 3 real sec; then 2.5 sec real -> 25 sim min, visitors spawn and move. So dynamic changes definitely. Good. B