>0. But pick after close already chose dest. callUp same. Good.\nCould also test during DOOR_OPEN after complete board and callUp(0) does not keep open; doors close. Then target5.\n\nTest 3:\n- e.callUp(0), open, board 1, press 4, callUp(0), tick repeatedly pressing callUp(0) maybe 50 ticks; assert eventually currentFloor===4 or state open at 4. But repeated pressing can add call while car travels. Our pick target already 4. Car reaches 4. But at arrival, destination 4 cleared, then up call 0 behind remains, after doors open at4, direction up, _hasStopsAhead? upCalls has 0 not ahead, so no; clear opposite down none. At close, direction up, ahead none -> reverse direction down, pool all calls (up0) -> target 0. Good. We assert reached 4. Good.\n\nTest 4 opposite-direction calls wait:\n- e.callUp(2), e.callUp(5), e.callDown(4) maybe car at 0. Direction after first pick? all calls: nearest 2 up. But down 4 higher. At floor2 open, direction up. clear up2. hasStopsAhead up: up5 -> yes, so down4 remains. Continue to 5. Assert before currentFloor reaches5 (while moving up), down call 4 not served / target>=5? Our pick after floor2: direction up, ahead candidates: up5 and dest none; down4 not matching, so target5. Good. Could assert while moving from2 to5 current target5 and direction1. Then eventually floor5. Fine.\n\nTest 5 door hold and safety cap:\n- e.callUp(0); open; reserve person but do not complete; tick until min open exceeded; assert state OPEN still. Then tick until MAX (18) -> state CLOSING. Need cap iterations. Add pendingDisembark? no.\n- Our tick with dt maybe .5. doorTimer. min=3. We tick 10 times .5 =5, state open. Then 40 times .5=20 -> closes. assert.\n\nTest 6 destination preserved:\n- e.callUp(0); open; reserve p; complete; e.pressDestination(5); e.callUp(0) leftover; tick until open at 5; assert state open currentFloor5. Good.\n\nTest 7 reset:\n- populate calls, destinations, passengers, pending, spot; reset; assert sizes0, dir0,target0,current0,state