{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":1317,"output":2120,"cacheRead":110464,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1280,"totalTokens":113901,"cost":{"input":0.00056927325,"output":0.0038584,"cacheRead":0.0080417792,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01246945245}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Major behavioral issue: WAITING_ELEVATOR count grows huge (42 of 60) and AT_DESK stays low. People spend huge time waiting, elevator continuously has riders 4 and destinations, but seems never enough. Why? At 600x, elevator cycles every few frames, should serve. But waiting 42 indicates maybe many agents are waiting at panels that never get accepted because of direction mismatch or capacity, and calls queue. Let's analyze.\n\nElevator at 4:42 floor0 DOWN DOOR_OPEN riders4 Dest[1,3,5], Up[0,1], Down[1,3,4,5]. Car direction DOWN at floor0 but destinations are above (1,3,5) and passengers 4? How can direction DOWN with destinations above? It arrived at 0 from above, opened, riders 4 disembark? But riders still 4, Dest above. At floor0, direction down; after door close, pick with passengers>0 and dests, direction down but ahead dests (floor<0) none -> chooses nearest dest overall -> 1, sets direction up. Fine. But why are there 4 riders at floor0? Perhaps they boarded going down? Actually riders going to 1,3,5 should be going up, but car direction down and at floor0. They might have boarded at floor0 and pressed upper floors, while car direction remains down until doors close. That's okay.\n\nThe bigger issue: WAITING_ELEVATOR 42. At 600x, the elevator might be serving but each agent's WAIT_AT_PANEL only accepts if isAcceptingAt direction matches. With lots of calls and full car, many wait. But over 90s (9 hours sim), should eventually. Some may be visitors doing office floor activities, but 42/60 is too many. Maybe there's a bug where agents get stuck waiting because car direction and hall call clearing: Up[0] persistent, and agents waiting on upper floors for down? Let's reason.\n\nLook at t=60: floor4 DOWN DOOR_OPEN riders4 Dest[0], Up[0], Down[1,2,3,4]. Waiting 42. Many down calls. Car serves down. But after floor4 open, riders exit and new riders board down. It goes to 0. Then at 0, up call, but car direction down; after doors close, pick: passengers maybe 0? destinations? If riders from upper floors all wanted 0, then no dest. direction down, ahead none, reverse up, pool all calls, nearest maybe up0? floor0 current; choice up0 at current -> _setTarget(0,'up') opens again. That might cause door reopen at floor0. Then leftover up callers board. But direction becomes up. Good.\n\nHowever why riders at floor0 with dest upper but direction down? After arriving 0 with dest0 cleared, passengers may still have upper dests if they boarded at floor0 earlier? Hmm.\n\nPotential bug: `WAIT_AT_PANEL` re-presses calls every frame. If car is at floor with DOOR_OPEN but direction mismatch, it keeps call. Fine.\n\nMaybe the issue is elevator only has 4 capacity and at 600x door cycles take 3+ frames? Each frame at 600x is 10 sim sec, door opening 1.2 sec => one tick; open min 3 sec => next tick could close if no pending. Waiting agents accept and enter within same frame? Sequence: frame N elevator.tick arrives OPENING; agent WAIT not accepted. Frame N+1 elevator.tick OPENING->OPEN; agent WAIT_AT_PANEL sees open and capacity free -> completes; next action ENTER starts reserve, phase door, moves huge step to threshold and phase inside, attaches, phase spot, moves huge, completeBoard. So boards in same frame. Great. But only up to 4. Then next frame elevator.tick sees pending empty (all complete) and doorTimer already? doorTimer at open was 0, then frame N+1 after elevator.tick state open timer 0. Agent boards. Frame N+2 elevator.tick doorTimer +=10 > min, pending 0 -> CLOSING. So car leaves. Good. So one floor per 3 frames per direction. At 600x, 3 frames=0.05s real, sim 30 sec. Should serve.\n\nBut maybe agents waiting for elevator are not at the car floor because their current action WAIT_AT_PANEL is stuck due direction mismatch and the car never comes to their floor in the matching direction. E.g., visitor at floor5 wants down, but car serves down calls only when direction down. It should. Yet call sets.\n\nCould be a more subtle bug: `WAIT_AT_PANEL` is pressed with dir based on toFloor, but action.floor may not equal agent.floor? In appendTravel, fromFloor is agent.floor at plan compile. If the agent's plan was compiled while in car or floor mismatch, maybe wrong. For planAttendMeeting: appendTravel(agent.floor,target). Agent.floor should be current. For planLeaveBuilding maybe. But wait counts huge.\n\nMaybe visitors top-up keeps spawning new visitors and their plans use upper floors; but 42 waiting is still too many.\n\nLet's inspect actual agent states/actions. Our sim variables are inside IIFE, not exposed. Could temporarily expose `window.__officeDebug = {agents, elevator, world, simClock}` for probing, then remove or keep harmless? It would help. We can add at end startSimulation `window.__officeDebug = ...`. Not forbidden. But final artifact maybe okay. Could expose for debugging. Better add temporary via edit then remove. But maybe we can infer.\n\nLet's expose and probe agents waiting: their floor, currentAction, toFloor, plan. Also elevator call sets. We'll add window.__officeDebug after buildHUD. Then probe after 60s. Use edit."}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":1317,"output":2120,"cacheRead":110464,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1280,"totalTokens":113901,"cost":{"input":0.00056927325,"output":0.0038584,"cacheRead":0.0080417792,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01246945245}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-99269305fc53c265","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('sim.js')\ns=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('''        buildHUD();\n        simClock.onNewDay = resetDay;''','''        buildHUD();\n        window.__officeDebug = {\n            agents: agents,\n            elevator: elevator,\n            world: world,\n            clock: simClock,\n            countPresent: countPresent\n        };\n        simClock.onNewDay = resetDay;''')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat > /tmp/office_debug.js <<'EOF'\nconst http=require('http'),fs=require('fs'),path=require('path');\nconst {chromium}=require('playwright');\nconst dir=process.argv[2];\nconst server=http.createServer((req,res)=>{let u=decodeURIComponent((req.url||'/').split('?')[0]);let f=path.join(dir,u==='/'?'index.html':u);fs.readFile(f,(e,d)=>{if(e){res.writeHead(404);res.end();return}res.writeHead(200,{'Content-Type':path.extname(f)==='.html'?'text/html':'text/javascript'});res.end(d)})});\nserver.listen(0,'127.0.0.1',async()=>{\n const port=server.address().port; const browser=await chromium.launch({headless:true}); const page=await browser.newPage({viewport:{width:1200,height:900}});\n const errors=[]; page.on('pageerror',e=>errors.push(e.message));\n await page.goto(`http://127.0.0.1:${port}/index.html`,{waitUntil:'domcontentloaded'}); await page.waitForTimeout(500);\n await page.evaluate(()=>{const ins=Array.from(document.querySelectorAll(\"input[type='range']\")); ins[0].value=ins[0].max; ins[0].dispatchEvent(new Event('input',{bubbles:true})); ins[1].value='60'; ins[1].dispatchEvent(new Event('input',{bubbles:true}));});\n await page.waitForTimeout(45000);\n const data=await page.evaluate(()=>{\n   const d=window.__officeDebug; const e=d.elevator;\n   const waiting=d.agents.filter(a=>a.state==='WAITING_ELEVATOR').map(a=>({name:a.name,role:a.role,id:a.id,floor:a.floor,action:a.currentAction&&{type:a.currentAction.type,floor:a.currentAction.floor,toFloor:a.currentAction.toFloor,dir:a.currentAction.dir},plan:(a.plan||[]).slice(0,4).map(x=>x.type+':'+(x.floor!==undefined?x.floor:'')+':'+(x.wp||x.toFloor||''))}));\n   const counts={}; d.agents.forEach(a=>counts[a.state]=(counts[a.state]||0)+1);\n   return {time:d.clock.format(), counts, waiting, elevator:{state:e.state,floor:e.currentFloor,target:e.targetFloor,dir:e.direction,up:[...e.upCalls],down:[...e.downCalls],dest:[...e.destinations],passengers:e.passengers.size,pendingB:e.pendingBoarders.size,pendingD:e.pendingDisembark.size}, seats:[...d.world.floors[0].nodes?[]:[]]};\n });\n console.log(JSON.stringify(data,null,2)); console.log('ERRORS',errors); await browser.close(); server.close();\n});\nEOF\nNODE_PATH=/home/jeff/Code/llm-eval/node_modules node /tmp/office_debug.js \"$PWD\"","timeout":120}}}}
