d over hall calls. Yes! Passenger destinations outrank hall calls. If riders want 0, car skips down hall calls 4,2,1 to serve 0, even though it passes floors. The spec says passenger destinations outrank same-floor hall calls, but not necessarily all hall calls; SCAN should serve matching-direction hall calls along the way, especially closer stops. Our `_pickNextTarget` when passengers>0 and dests picks nearest destination, ignoring matching hall calls ahead. This causes starvation of hall calls when riders' destination is 0: car always goes straight to 0, then at 0 takes new riders, then their destinations maybe upper, skipping down calls again on return? On return up it ignores down calls (opposite) and serves up. Down calls never get served because car passes them while going down with dest0 and ignores. At 0, direction down, reverses up. It never opens at intermediate down floors. That's the bug.\n\nNeed modify logic: when passengers>0 and destinations, choose among destinations and matching-direction hall calls ahead (or nearest destination if none). But requirement \"Passenger destinations outrank same-floor hall calls\" specifically same-floor. We can include matching hall calls in same direction as candidates. At floor5 direction down, passengers dest0, down calls4,2,1: ahead matching down calls exist, choose nearest floor4 (hall call) rather than dest0. This serves down calls. But careful: if passenger destination is 5 (up) and same-floor call 5? no. For same-floor hall call at current floor, dests outrank. Our selection of ahead candidates can include dests and matching hall calls, but exclude current floor. This matches SCAN.\n\nNeed ensure test 1 (lobby rush) still passes: at floor0 after board, direction? It was inferred +1 from up call at open. After close, passengers dests above, direction up, ahead candidates include dests above and matching up hall calls above. Leftover callUp(0) at current floor excluded. Choose nearest dest. Good.\nTest 2 same floor call: direction up, dest4, callUp0 current -> ahead candidates dest4 only (floor0 excluded) -> dest. Good.\nTest 3 callUp0 repeatedly while car moves: at each close, current maybe0; ahead dest4. Later after serving dest4 and at floor4 direction up, dest maybe none, up0 behind; passengers maybe 0 after disembark. It can reverse to0. Fine.\nTest 4 no passengers, unchanged.\n\nSo modify `_pickNextTarget` passenger branch:\n```\nif passengers>0 && dests.length {\n let ahead = [];\n if dir>0 ahead = all.filter(item => item.floor>current && (item.kind==='dest'||item.kind==='up'));\n else if dir<0 ahead = all.filter(item => item.floor<current && (item.kind==='dest'||item.kind==='down'));\n else ahead = dests;\n if ahead.length) choice nearest ahead; _setTarget(choice.floor, choice.kind)\n else { choose nearest dest (reverse) }\n return\n}\n```\nShould a matching hall call ahead outrank a farther dest? Nearest ahead works. If hall call at4 and dest0, serves4 then continue. Good.\n\nBut there is nuance: if a passenger destination is floor5 and there is an up hall call at2, it will stop at2. Good.\n\nAlso `_reconsiderWhileMoving` already includes dests and matching calls, so it would have retargeted closer hall calls! Wait it does consider down calls while moving down. At floor5 target0, moving down, it calls `_reconsiderWhileMoving`, which considers downCalls floors4,2,1 and dest0, picks nearest floor4 and sets target4. So why didn't it? Because at pick at floor5, direction maybe UP? Debug t4: floor5 MOVING target0 dir -1. If direction -1, reconsider should retarget to4. Maybe car had already passed 4 before calls were pressed? down calls [2,1,4] at t4. It may have picked target0 at floor5 before down4 call was added? No, down4 was present. Hmm. Let's re-examine: `_reconsiderWhileMoving` is called every tick; it considers `calls = dir>0? upCalls: downCalls`. It should see down4 and carY=5, dist1 < target0 dist5, retarget4. Unless direction was +1 when picking target0? Debug says dir -1 at t4. But perhaps target0 was chosen when direction was down and `_reconsider` did retarget to4, opened at4, then after serving 4, passengers dest0 remains, pickNext with passenger branch chooses nearest dest0, ignoring down2,1; then passes 2,1 because reconsider? It should reconsider and stop at2,1. So maybe it did and debug snapshot caught it after? Down calls still [2,1,4] at t4 though, so no.\n\nWait `_reconsiderWhileMoving` only retargets if `bestDist < bestDist - 1e-6` where bestDist initialized abs(target-y). If target0 and y=5, bestDist5; down4 dist1 -> target4. Should. Unless car was already at y=0? Debug floor5 target0 at moment MOVING just after leaving 5 maybe. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the issue is down calls are added after car passes them. E.g., car leaves 5 toward0, passes4 quickly at 600x in one tick (travelSpeed 2.6*10=26 floors), so it jumps from5 to0 in one tick before any reconsider? `_reconsiderWhileMoving` is called before moving each tick; at tick from y5, calls down4 present -> retarget4. Then move 26 floors to target4 in same tick, arrives, opens. So it should serve4. Debug t4 says target0, so maybe down4 was pressed after car already at/near0 but then car would be floor0. Hmm.\n\nLet's instrument logic quickly in Node with scenario: passengers dest0 at floor5, down calls 4,2,1 added, see target. But likely the passenger branch picks dest0 at door close, then next tick reconsider should fix. At dt huge, first tick after close: state MOVING target0, carY5; reconsider retarget4; move to4 and open. So target4. Fine. Maybe debug is from moment after car left 5 toward0 where down calls got added after it passed 4 due high speed? At 600x, in a single tick it can move 26 floors, so if a down call at4 is pressed during same frame after elevator.tick, the car may have already passed 4 and be at0. Then call4 remains behind. But car at0 then goes up; down4 gets served on next down trip. Not starvation.\n\nThe persistent down calls at 1,2,3,5 with car often up might still resolve. But stayed waiting 20 across 3s suggests some agents wait very long. Maybe they are waiting for down at floors that are repeatedly passed. Let's look at one stuck ID across samples. Modify probe to track same IDs and their toFloor. But we already saw e.g. waiting 25 -> stayed20 means most waiting remained after 3s (30 sim min). That's a lot. Could be due continuous new calls, but same IDs.\n\nLet's patch passenger branch and retest. Also consider the hall call clearing at floor when direction up and down call same floor: it doesn't clear down until no up stops ahead. That's spec. Fine.\n\nPatch logic."}}
