{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still lots waiting. But maybe because at 600x with 60 people and 4 capacity, and continuous visitor cycling, there is genuine demand overload. Let's compute: Each elevator trip takes maybe 4 floors * (1/2.6 sim sec) + door ~4+ sec = ~6 sim sec? At 600x, 6 sim sec =0.01s real. Capacity4, so ~400 people/sim? Not bottleneck. But our elevator at 600x with dt ~10 sim sec per frame takes one state transition per frame. Door opening (1 frame), open (1 frame), closing (1 frame), moving (1 frame), = 4 frames per floor stop. At 60fps, 15 stops/sec real. Each stop boards max4, so 60 people/sec. Should drain 60 in 1s. Yet waiting persists 30s. Something else.\n\nMaybe waiting agents are not being served because they never reach the car due to collision? State WAITING means they are at panel, but ENTER_ELEVATOR only starts when isAcceptingAt and capacity. If car opens at floor and accepts direction, multiple waiting agents (maybe 20) all complete WAIT in same frame and start ENTER. First 4 reserve spots, others call reserve returns null and wait in ENTER phase 'reserve'. They have currentAction ENTER_ELEVATOR, state? We never set state in ENTER; remains WAITING_ELEVATOR from prior action. So HUD counts them WAITING_ELEVATOR even though they're in reserve phase. They remain there until car returns. But they are not counted as pendingBoarders. On next car arrival, they may reserve. This is okay but explains waiting count includes queued boarders.\n\nHowever why 30 still? Let's inspect individual waiting IDs over time. The stayed count 26 might be the same agents. Perhaps their currentAction is ENTER_ELEVATOR reserve, not WAIT_AT_PANEL, and they are stuck because `isAcceptingAt` never true for them? In ENTER reserve phase, they re-press call. They should eventually. Let's inspect action types of waiting. Our earlier debug showed WAIT_AT_PANEL for all waiting. But that was before patch. Let's get distribution of currentAction types and maybe one stuck agent's floor/toFloor and elevator direction over time. Also track if any agent's `state` is WAITING but action ENTER. Use debug.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Still lots waiting. But maybe because at 600x with 60 people and 4 capacity, and continuous visitor cycling, there is genuine demand overload. Let's compute: Each elevator trip takes maybe 4 floors * (1/2.6 sim sec) + door ~4+ sec = ~6 sim sec? At 600x, 6 sim sec =0.01s real. Capacity4, so ~400 people/sim? Not bottleneck. But our elevator at 600x with dt ~10 sim sec per frame takes one state transition per frame. Door opening (1 frame), open (1 frame), closing (1 frame), moving (1 frame), = 4 frames per floor stop. At 60fps, 15 stops/sec real. Each stop boards max4, so 60 people/sec. Should drain 60 in 1s. Yet waiting persists 30s. Something else.\\n\\nMaybe waiting agents are not being served because they never reach the car due to collision? State WAITING means they are at panel, but ENTER_ELEVATOR only starts when isAcceptingAt and capacity. If car opens at floor and accepts direction, multiple waiting agents (maybe 20) all complete WAIT in same frame and start ENTER. First 4 reserve spots, others call reserve returns null and wait in ENTER phase 'reserve'. They have currentAction ENTER_ELEVATOR, state? We never set state in ENTER; remains WAITING_ELEVATOR from prior action. So HUD counts them WAITING_ELEVATOR even though they're in reserve phase. They remain there until car returns. But they are not counted as pendingBoarders. On next car arrival, they may reserve. This is okay but explains waiting count includes queued boarders.\\n\\nHowever why 30 still? Let's inspect individual waiting IDs over time. The stayed count 26 might be the same agents. Perhaps their currentAction is ENTER_ELEVATOR reserve, not WAIT_AT_PANEL, and they are stuck because `isAcceptingAt` never true for them? In ENTER reserve phase, they re-press call. They should eventually. Let's inspect action types of waiting. Our earlier debug showed WAIT_AT_PANEL for all waiting. But that was before patch. Let's get distribution of currentAction types and maybe one stuck agent's floor/toFloor and elevator direction over time. Also track if any agent's `state` is WAITING but action ENTER. Use debug.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a02fb372eb73fe5","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cat > /tmp/office_stuck2.js <<'EOF'\nconst http=require('http'),fs=require('fs'),path=require('path');\nconst {chromium}=require('playwright');\nconst dir=process.argv[2];\nconst server=http.createServer((req,res)=>{let u=decodeURIComponent((req.url||'/').split('?')[0]);let f=path.join(dir,u==='/'?'index.html':u);fs.readFile(f,(e,d)=>{if(e){res.writeHead(404);res.end();return}res.writeHead(200,{'Content-Type':path.extname(f)==='.html'?'text/html':'text/javascript'});res.end(d)})});\nserver.listen(0,'127.0.0.1',async()=>{\n const port=server.address().port; const browser=await chromium.launch({headless:true}); const page=await browser.newPage({viewport:{width:1200,height:900}});\n await page.goto(`http://127.0.0.1:${port}/index.html`,{waitUntil:'domcontentloaded'}); await page.waitForTimeout(500);\n await page.evaluate(()=>{const ins=Array.from(document.querySelectorAll(\"input[type='range']\")); ins[0].value=ins[0].max; ins[0].dispatchEvent(new Event('input',{bubbles:true})); ins[1].value='60'; ins[1].dispatchEvent(new Event('input',{bubbles:true}));});\n await page.waitForTimeout(40000);\n const track=[];\n for(let k=0;k<12;k++){\n   await page.waitForTimeout(1000);\n   const d=await page.evaluate(()=>{const d=window.__officeDebug;const e=d.elevator;const waiting=d.agents.filter(a=>a.state==='WAITING_ELEVATOR');const types={};waiting.forEach(a=>{const t=a.currentAction?a.currentAction.type:'none';types[t]=(types[t]||0)+1});return {time:d.clock.format(),waiting:waiting.map(a=>({id:a.