 arrival/departure, deficit won't be filled. This could reduce population later. In our long probe at 600x occupancy60, present ~55-60, so pool still works. But let's reason: when a visitor spawns, state ARRIVING, then plan -> EXIT_BUILDING -> GONE. topUp re-arms GONE. AWAY with future arrival not skipped? topUp skips if arrivalTime <= now+15 (imminent), so it won't rearm them and they will spawn soon. AWAY with past arrival but departure past: maybe this occurs if visitor was re-armed at e.g. now+6, then topUp next frame sees arrival <= now+15 skip; they spawn at arrival if now <= departure+10. If the simulation frame jumps (600x, 10 sim min per frame), a visitor with arrival now+6 and visitDuration 30 has departure arrival+30; maybeSpawn at now+10 (<=departure+10) spawns. Fine. If visitDuration small 30, okay. If arrival rearmed and then topUp skipped, maybeSpawn should catch within 40 min window. At high speed frame jumps 10 min, still within. So no permanent AWAY. At day start initial visitor arrival 8:00-10:00 and departure arrival+duration 30-100; maybeSpawn window. Fine.\nBut if an AWAY visitor's arrival passed during a long pause or at day reset? At reset, resample initial arrival 8:00-10:00, departure arrival+duration. At 8:00 topUp may rearm them if arrival>now+15. If arrival within 15 min, they spawn later. Fine. At 18:00 topUp stops; any AWAY with future arrival maybe >18? Initial max10:00. No. So okay.\n\nPotential bug: topUp business hours now<8*60 or >18*60 return. At exactly 8:00 okay. Visitors arriving after 18 not rearmed. Good.\n\nPotential bug: `applyOccupancy` reducing occupancy for GONE sets DISABLED and removes group. For active agents left running; on GONE after finishing, they won't automatically become DISABLED because applyOccupancy only called on slider input. Spec says \"they'll finish naturally, reach GONE, and only be parked DISABLED on the next day-wrap.\" So that's fine; they stay GONE and countPresent excludes. topUp loops only visitors id<target. Good.\nIncreasing occupancy from lower: DISABLED->AWAY but arrivalTime may be in past and departure past; maybeSpawn for worker checks now>departure -> skip; visitor maybe skip; topUp will rearm GONE/AWAY visitors but workers stuck AWAY until next day. Spec says slider moves agents between AWAY and DISABLED; if re-enable workers mid-day maybe they should arrive. Our workers with arrivalTime past and departure future will spawn (maybeSpawn now>=arrival && now<=departure). If now after departure, skip. Acceptable. Visitors rearm. Fine.\n\nPotential bug: `buildAgents` assigns workers first 20 ids. Occupancy slider min1: first agent worker enabled. If occupancy e.g. 10 only workers; no visitors. Fine.\n\nPotential bug: worker homeFloor assignment: deskPool iterates floors1..5, 4 desks each, workers 0-19. Good.\n\nPotential bug: office desk seat orientation facing PI; chair at z-6.1, desk at z-7.35. Legs local +Z with rotation PI -> world -Z toward desk. yes.\n\nPotential bug: In SIT, when target.sit false, jitter ring could put person at radius 0.75 around elevWait and collide with crowd, but fine.\n\nPotential bug: collision pushes agents outside building/walls because no wall collision. Could push through exterior? Only agent-agent repulsion near doors; not huge. Fine.\n\nPotential bug: while agents walk, `agent.group.position.y = agent.floor*FH`; if they are in car and walking? No WALK inside car except ENTER spot custom. EXIT after scene attach. Fine.\n\nPotential bug: When agent finishes WALK_TO_WP to office door, state ON_FLOOR; next WALK desk start sets state? startAction sees state ON_FLOOR, doesn't change. Fine.\nAt plan start from desk SIT, state AT_DESK. Next action STAND leaves state AT_DESK; next WALK start changes to ON_FLOOR. good.\nAt plan start STAND when not sitting, still y restored.\n\nPotential bug: `planWorkAtDesk` called when agent at desk but current state AT_DESK and sitting; it appends WALK deskDoor, causing them to stand up and walk to door then back to desk for no reason. In chooseNextActivity \"rest: WAIT_SIM + another decision later (keep working)\" should just wait at desk, not walk. Our planWorkAtDesk always walks to deskDoor and back. This means every \"keep working\" decision makes the worker get up, walk to office door, then back to desk. That's odd behavior and extra elevator? No, same floor. It could cause unnecessary motion and queue but not huge. However it may look like people constantly getting up and walking to doors. We should optimize: if agent is already at home floor and state AT_DESK, plan just WAIT_SIM + PICK_NEXT_ACTIVITY. But after a lounge/meeting return, we already explicitly sit at desk before WAIT. So planWorkAtDesk is only called from chooseNextActivity when agent is at desk (or fallback from no coworker). In both cases likely at desk. So change planWorkAtDesk:\n```\nif (agent.floor===agent.homeFloor && agent.state==='AT_DESK') return [WAIT_SIM(18..65), PICK_NEXT_ACTIVITY];\nelse existing travel + walk...\n```\nThis avoids silly pacing. Also if state AT_DESK but not sitting? SIT already done. Good. If fallback from planVisitCoworker while at desk, state AT_DESK. Good. If chooseNextActivity called when visitor? no.\n\nLet's patch."}}
