loor, after close pick dest at current? rare. Not important.\n\nPotential issue: Door open logic clears destinations at floor and hall call for current direction. If no stops ahead current direction, clears opposite call at this floor. Good.\nBut when car arrives at floor with both a destination and a hall call opposite direction while full, it clears destination, keeps opposite call if stops ahead current direction. Fine.\n\nPotential issue: `isAcceptingAt` returns true if direction 0 regardless. When idle opens at floor due call, direction inferred before opening, so not 0 usually. If callUp at floor but current direction maybe from previous? fine.\n\nPotential issue: in `_pickNextTarget`, if passengers>0 and dests and direction 0 (could happen after reset? no, if direction not set because passenger manually added) uses dests. good.\n\nPotential issue: Test required scenario 5 door hold: \"doors remain open while pendingBoarders or pendingDisembark are non-empty after minimum open time, but close after MAX if something never completes.\" yes.\n\nPotential issue: `completeBoard` when person has reservation and pending; after move to passengers, spot stays occupied. On force close pendingBoarders cleared only. Fine.\n\nPotential issue: `reserveBoardingSpot` doesn't verify person already pending; if called twice for same person, could allocate two spots and overwrite map. Sim guarantees once. Tests not. Fine.\n\nCould make robust: if pendingBoarders.has(person) return existing spot. Not necessary but good. Also if passengers.has(person), maybe return null. Let's add simple guard? Not needed.\n\nPotential issue: static check contract only for wiggum, but maybe evaluator uses general static. Good.\n\nPotential issue: index loads Three 0.147.0 from cdn. Runtime worked with network. good.\n\nPotential issue: No ES modules. yes.\n\nPotential issue: \"No build process\". yes.\n\nPotential issue: \"Do not add extra local files such as app.js\" only required six+html. We have exactly these plus check jsons. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"Do NOT look at other implementations.\" We did not.\n\nNow final run full tests after planWork change.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Another potential oddity: chooseNextActivity ad-hoc meeting 14% can happen frequently. Fine.\\nWorkers after meeting return to desk and WAIT, then choose. Good.\\n\\nPotential issue: Worker planGoToLunch after lunch returns to desk and WAIT. hasLunched marked before travel. If lunch travel takes long, still no repeat. Good.\\nIf lunch seat unavailable fallback cafe_order stand; MARK_LUNCHED. Good.\\n\\nPotential issue: `planVisitLounge` from desk starts STAND, RELEASE, then WALK lounge seat. At end walks deskDoor then desk. Good.\\n`planAttendMeeting` if targetFloor == homeFloor, appendTravel no-op, then WALK conf_center from desk direct BFS. Good.\\nIf targetFloor different, appendTravel from desk floor to target begins WALK elevWait, BFS from desk to elevWait. It may pick nearest node to desk (desk node) and path desk->door->hallN...->elevWait. good.\\nAt end appendTravel(target, home) begins WALK elevWait from conf seat, BFS. good.\\n`planVisitCoworker` similar.\\n\\nOne bug: For visitors, `planVisitorVisit` upper-floor meeting branch reserves a conference seat. Then appendTravel(0, upper) and later appendTravel(upper,0). Fine. But if visitor's `EXIT_ELEVATOR` target floor and then WALK_TO_WP conf center, okay.\\n\\nPotential bug: `planVisitorVisit` for bistro branch reserves seat at compile while visitor is still outside. Another agent could plan and reserve. fine.\\n\\nPotential bug: `findFreeSeat` returns null if all reserved; then fallback to stand. Good.\\n\\nOne concern: Seat reservations for conference seats are made at plan compile but visitor may be far away (outside) and reservation could sit idle for a while, reducing availability. Acceptable.\\n\\nPotential issue: Elevator logic `_setTarget` when floor===current and kind \\\"dest\\\" does not reset direction; if direction stale opposite, isAcceptingAt might reject callers even though no stops ahead? `_hasStopsAhead` maybe. At current floor, after close pick dest at current? rare. Not important.\\n\\nPotential issue: Door open logic clears destinations at floor and hall call for current direction. If no stops ahead current direction, clears opposite call at this floor. Good.\\nBut when car arrives at floor with both a destination and a hall call opposite direction while full, it clears destination, keeps opposite call if stops ahead current direction. Fine.\\n\\nPotential issue: `isAcceptingAt` returns true if direction 0 regardless. When idle opens at floor due call, direction inferred before opening, so not 0 usually. If callUp at floor but current direction maybe from previous? fine.\\n\\nPotential issue: in `_pickNextTarget`, if passengers>0 and dests and direction 0 (could happen after reset? no, if direction not set because passenger manually added) uses dests. good.\\n\\nPotential issue: Test required scenario 5 door hold: \\\"doors remain open while pendingBoarders or pendingDisembark are non-empty after minimum open time, but close after MAX if something never completes.\\\" yes.\\n\\nPotential issue: `completeBoard` when person has reservation and pending; after move to passengers, spot stays occupied. On force close pendingBoarders cleared only. Fine.\\n\\nPotential issue: `reserveBoardingSpot` doesn't verify person already pending; if called twice for same person, could allocate two spots and overwrite map. Sim guarantees once. Tests not. Fine.\\n\\nCould make robust: if pendingBoarders.has(person) return existing spot. Not necessary but good. Also if passengers.has(person), maybe return null. Let's add simple guard? Not needed.\\n\\nPotential issue: static check contract only for wiggum, but maybe evaluator uses general static. Good.\\n\\nPotential issue: index loads Three 0.147.0 from cdn. Runtime worked with network. good.\\