nf seat, sit wait 20..40, release, return down.\n  Then exit chain: WALK lobby_center, entrance, threshold, outside, EXIT_BUILDING.\n  For office floor activity need elevator both ways. Build helper appendTravel(actions, fromFloor,toFloor,dir). Since plan sequence known.\n\nWe can create helper `pushTravel(agent, actions, fromFloor, toFloor)` that appends WALK_TO_WP(fromFloor,'elevWait'), WAIT_AT_PANEL(fromFloor, dir, toFloor), ENTER_ELEVATOR(toFloor), PRESS_FLOOR(toFloor), WAIT_FOR_FLOOR(toFloor), EXIT_ELEVATOR(toFloor). But if fromFloor==toFloor skip. This requires agent currently on floor. At plan compile time known. Good. But when plan starts from desk, need first walk deskDoor before elevWait. BFS from desk position to elevWait direct might work. We can just WALK_TO_WP(fromFloor,'elevWait') from seat; BFS starts nearest node (desk seat) to elevWait, fine. For leaving desk, STAND first. Good.\n\nHowever for arrival plan from lobby_center to elevator we can explicit. For visitor activity after walking in, at lobby_center then pushTravel to floor. Fine.\n\nFor meeting plan from desk: STAND then WALK_TO_WP(homeFloor,'elevWait') direct BFS from desk; no need deskDoor. But BFS from nearest node to desk maybe path desk->door->hall. Good. We'll still include deskDoor? Direct BFS through door node works since desk linked to door. Good.\n\nBut WALK_TO_WP uses BFS from nearest node, and if agent is at seat (desk node) fine.\n\nWhen SIT desk, node position maybe at chair; legs orientation. Good.\n\nBistro seats floor0, sit targets.\n\nReservations: helper reserveSeat(floor, wp) uses key `${floor}:${wp}`, checks seatReservations. Adds and agent.reservedSeats push. Release removes. For plans, reserve at compile time. If activity fails no seat fallback. Workers returning desk don't reserve. Lounge visitors reserve. Conference. Bistro. Pit/back lounge. Good. Could two workers plan lounge same seat? reserve prevents. If all reserved, fallback water cooler stand.\n\nNeed release