ess = state DOOR_OPEN/OPENING => 1, CLOSING maybe based on timer, else 0. Simplest: state DOOR_OPEN => 1, DOOR_OPENING => min(1, doorTimer/openTime), DOOR_CLOSING => 1 - timer/closeTime. Need expose doorTimer/openTime. Fine.\\n\\nIndicators: create text texture functions maybe in world.js but can duplicate in elevator.js? Need avoid duplicate top-level const names across files. Use unique names prefixed. We can define makeTextTexture in world.js global `makeDisplayTexture` and use from elevator.js. But static checker cross-file project globals resolves. Better world.js expose `window.createDisplayTexture`. Then elevator uses. But if world.js loaded before elevator yes. Need careful.\\n\\nCall panel updates in elevator tick: for each floor callPanel.setUp(upCalls.has(f)), setDown; setIndicator(currentFloor + direction symbol). Shaft indicator set text e.g. `${currentFloor}${direction>0?'^':direction<0?'v':' '}`. Requirement show current floor and direction. Use ascii maybe font handles ^. Fine.\\n\\nIn-car indicator current floor + arrow. Destination buttons: light if destinations has floor or current? We'll light if logic.destinations.has(f) || currentFloor===f. Buttons cylinders.\\n\\nAdapter methods delegate. Also need world.floors panels.\\n\\nCar reparenting: In sim ENTER_ELEVATOR, spec says reparent scene -> car. Use car.group.attach(person.group) after threshold? We'll implement in sim using elevator.group (car). Ensure world y transforms. We'll expose elevator.carGroup. Agent positions.\\n\\nPerson local coordinates inside car: spots x,z local, y 0. We'll move to target local position. When exiting, reparent to scene via scene.attach(group) preserving world position, then set y floor*FH, walk to elevWait.\\n\\nElevator car moves every tick; attached people move with it.\\n\\nSim.js major.\\n\\nClock: object with simMinute, timeScale, tick(realDt), format. Need day wrap callback resetting agents and elevator. Could implement Clock class with onNewDay callback.