if agent is at seat (desk node) fine.\\n\\nWhen SIT desk, node position maybe at chair; legs orientation. Good.\\n\\nBistro seats floor0, sit targets.\\n\\nReservations: helper reserveSeat(floor, wp) uses key `${floor}:${wp}`, checks seatReservations. Adds and agent.reservedSeats push. Release removes. For plans, reserve at compile time. If activity fails no seat fallback. Workers returning desk don't reserve. Lounge visitors reserve. Conference. Bistro. Pit/back lounge. Good. Could two workers plan lounge same seat? reserve prevents. If all reserved, fallback water cooler stand.\\n\\nNeed release in plan. For fallback no reservation.\\n\\nPotential leak if agent leaves/dies; releaseAgentSeats in reset/exit/depart override.\\n\\nSeat reservations at plan compile for visitor meetings. Fine.\\n\\nNow collision:\\napplyCollisions:\\nFor each pair i<j, both in scene graph, same parent (scene or car). skip if either isSitting, currentAction.type ENTER_ELEVATOR or EXIT_ELEVATOR, or parent is car (skip all car). Also maybe skip agents disabled/invisible. Compute dx,dz, dy difference <1.0? \\\"same parent within ~1 unit of Y and ~0.7 of XZ\\\". Actually distance XZ < PERSON_R*2? Use minDist=0.65? PERSON_R=0.4 -> 0.8. Use 0.8. If d<0.001 random separation. Push each by 0.18 * overlap? Spec low push scalar 0.18. Compute push = (minDist-d)*0.18 maybe too low but okay. Apply half each? Use 0.18 each. Clamp positions within building? maybe not. Avoid pushing into walls not modeled. Fine.\\n\\nNeed walking agents progress; collisions may push. Stall skip.\\n\\nTop-level `let` uniqueness: We'll use functions and consts unique. person.js has no top-level const perhaps palettes as const SHIRT_PALETTE etc. world.js const WORLD; material vars maybe const. elevator.js top-level class Elevator. sim.js many consts; ensure no duplicate with world/elevator. Avoid `const FLOOR_HEIGHT` in sim. Use WORLD.FLOOR_HEIGHT. Names unique.\\n\\nStatic checker project globals includes window assignmen