, clear opposite at this floor. Good.\n\nPotential: at floor0 up call, direction inferred +1, clears up. no ahead, clears down. fine.\n\n`_hasStopsAhead(dir)` returns true if any destination floor ahead or upCalls ahead (dir>0) or downCalls ahead. If dir=0 false.\n\nisAcceptingAt: if state DOOR_OPEN current floor. if direction 0 true. if caller dir===this.direction true. else if !_hasStopsAhead(this.direction) true. But if current direction up and no up stops ahead but down call at this floor was cleared at open, a down caller can board (accept) and press dest. Fine.\n\nDoor open tick:\n```\nif (state DOOR_OPEN) {\n doorTimer += dt;\n const pending = pendingBoarders.size + pendingDisembark.size;\n if (pending===0 && doorTimer>=MIN) {state=DOOR_CLOSING; doorTimer=0;}\n else if (doorTimer>=MAX) { // force close\n   // clear pending boarders and disembark? release spots\n   this.pendingBoarders.forEach((spot,p)=>{if(spotOccupancy[spot.index]===p) spotOccupancy[spot.index]=null;});\n   this.pendingBoarders.clear();\n   this.pendingDisembark.clear();\n   state=DOOR_CLOSING; doorTimer=0;\n }\n}\n```\nShould we clear pendingDisembark on forced close? If a passenger is mid-exit and not complete, closing leaves them passenger and still in car; maybe not good but safety. Tests only close. We'll clear pendingBoarders only, keep pendingDisembark? If kept, next open might. But safety cap should close even if something never completes. Clear both and leave passengers set? Then passengers stuck but can exit later. Could remove pending disembark from passengers? Hmm. We'll clear pendingDisembark, leave passenger in passengers. That's okay.\n\nDoor closing tick: after DOOR_CLOSE_TIME, state='IDLE', servedThisDoorCycle=false; then immediately `_pickNextTarget()` maybe sets MOVING/OPENING. If IDLE and target same floor leftover call, opens. Good. But `servedThisDoorCycle` maybe not needed after reset. Keep.\n\nIDLE tick: if calls/dests exist pick. Also if current floor has dest/call and no? pick handles. If no work state IDLE.\n\nMOVING tick and re-evaluate: need account door states.\n\n`_chooseNearest(list, current)`: choose min abs floor-current; tie prefer dest.\n\nOne issue: pick after closing with leftover same floor hall call and no passengers may open again immediately; fine capacity available. But if car full of passengers (passengers>0, dests) chooses dest.\n\nDoor opening time and closing time count. Tick dt could be huge 9.6; state transitions one per tick. Door opening takes one tick, then door open next, etc. At 600x this means doors take ~3 frames ~50ms real, okay. Boarders might only have one frame DOOR_OPEN before min elapses? MIN 3 < dt 9.6, but pendingBoarders holds. Good.\n\nNeed tick while DOOR_OPENING: if doorTimer>=DOOR_OPEN_TIME -> _openDoors. If dt huge, okay.\n\nAlso if state IDLE at floor and calls at current, pick opens.\n\nLet's write file with tests later.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Concern: addChair function `const seat` etc void to avoid lint but not needed. Fine. Also top-level `function createDisplayTexture` is inside IIFE, window assigned. static checker sees function declaration inside IIFE scope, not global projectGlobals? It will parse window.createDisplayTexture assignment adds project global. Good.\\n\\nBut floor slabs: front strip z center computed `1.5 + (D/2-1.5)/2` =1.5+3.75=5.25, depth 7.5 -> z1.5..9. good. back -5.25. left/right x center ±(1.5+ (11-1.5)/2)=±6.25 width 9.5 -> 1.5..11. good.\\n\\nPotential entrance doorway: front wall side panels from x -11..-1.5 and 1.5..11, header above floor0. Glass doors at x ±2.15 outside gap? Door width1.4 rotated, may extend into gap? left center -2.15, rotated 1.15 rad extends x maybe ~0.57 half width + thickness; reaches -1.58, outside gap boundary -1.5 maybe slight. Visual only, okay. No physical collision anyway.\\n\\nNow elevator_logic.js. Implement thoroughly. Need plain object spot.\\n\\nLet's write.\\n\\nConstants insid