te. Compute hasStopsAhead.\\nSpec: true only when at floor DOOR_OPEN AND either no more stops pending in current direction OR caller's direction matches car's. So if hasStopsAhead(dir) then direction must equal. But also if caller dir is opposite while car direction up but no up work left, true. If car direction up and up work remains, a down caller at this floor should not board. Good.\\nNeed hasStopsAhead(direction) includes destinations or hall calls strictly ahead in direction. If direction 0 maybe check both. Implement.\\n\\nPick next target at door close / idle:\\n```\\n_pickNextTarget() {\\n const current=this.currentFloor;\\n const hasDest=this.destinations.size>0;\\n const candidates=[];\\n dests -> {floor, kind:'dest'}\\n upCalls -> {floor, kind:'up'}\\n downCalls -> {floor, kind:'down'}\\n if none: direction=0; target=current; state='IDLE'; return;\\n // passenger dests outrank hall calls\\n let pool;\\n if (passengers.size>0 && hasDest) pool = destCandidates;\\n else if (this.direction!==0) {\\n   // ahead in dir: dest + matching hall call\\n   const ahead = candidates.filter(c => (dir>0 ? c.floor>current : c.floor<current) && (c.kind==='dest' || (dir>0?c.kind==='up':c.kind==='down')));\\n   if (ahead.length) pool=ahead;\\n   else {\\n      // reverse\\n      this.direction = -this.direction;\\n      pool = candidates; // nearest any\\n   }\\n } else {\\n   pool=candidates;\\n }\\n if pool empty...\\n choose nearest floor; tie prefer destination.\\n set targetFloor=floor.\\n infer direction: if floor>current ->1; if floor<current -> -1; if floor===current -> direction from candidate kind or existing.\\n if floor===current:\\n    // open doors unless servedThisDoorCycle? served false after close.\\n    this.targetFloor=current;\\n    this.state='DOOR_OPENING'; this.doorTimer=0; // But if servedThisDoorCycle true? reset at close.\\n else state='MOVING'\\n}\\n```\\nNeed avoid opening same floor when there are passenger destinations? pool dests only, if dest floor===current? Those should have been cleared at open. If not, open and clear. fine.\\n\\nWhen direction nonzero and ahead empty, reversing then pool = candidates nearest any including calls behind; but passenger destinations outrank? If passengers>0 and hasDest and none ahead, should choose nearest dest behind (reverse) not hall call. Our early condition only handles passengers>0 && hasDest with all dests, ignoring direction, choosing nearest dest overall. That could reverse even when there is up hall call ahead and passenger dest behind. Which is better? Passenger destinations outrank hall calls, yes. So if passengers >0 and any destinations, choose nearest dest (regardless direction). Then direction inferred. This may not maintain direction but okay. Tests likely expect. However scenario 4 opposite-direction calls wait while moving UP with work above and passengers destinations? If passenger dest above nearest, chooses above. If passenger dest below and up hall calls above, spec says passenger destinations outrank same-floor hall calls, but direction handling maybe should continue? It says \\\"At each door-close ... prefer continuing in current direction: nearest destination or matching-direction hall call ahead. If no work remains ahead, reverse...\\\". And \\\"Passenger destinations outrank same-floor hall calls.\\\" Not all hall calls. Hmm tests may set passengers destinations above. Fine.\\n\\nBetter algorithm:\\n- If passengers>0 and dests:\\n   aheadDest = dests ahead in current dir (if direction !=0)\\n   if aheadDest length -> choose nearest ahead dest\\n   else if direction==0 -> nearest dest\\n   else {\\n      // no dest ahead; could still serve matching hall calls ahead before reversing? SCAN would continue current direction for hall calls even if passenger destinations behind? Passengers should not be taken past their destination ideally. But passengers already aboard; their destination behind means car overshot? shouldn't happen. We can choose nearest dest (reverse).\\n   }\\n- else direction etc.\\n\\nTo satisfy test 2 same-floor hall call: dests nonempty. choose dest. Fine.\\nTest 1 dest above; choose above.\\nTest 3 repeated callUp(0) while riders dest; choose dest.\\nTest 4 moving UP with work above, down call lower. We should not reverse. If passengers empty, direction up and ahead has up calls/dests -> choose ahead. Good.\\n\\nLet's implement pick:\\n```\\nconst destList = [...destinations].map...\\nconst allCalls...\\nif (passengers.size>0 && destList.length) {\\n  let aheadDest = dir>0 ? dests>current : dir<0 ? dests<current : [];\\n  if (dir===0) choose nearest dest\\n  else if (aheadDest.length) choose nearest aheadDest\\n  else choose nearest dest // reverse if needed\\n  setTarget...\\n  return\\n}\\nif (this.direction!==0) {\\n  const ahead = candidates.filter(c => (dir>0 ? c.floor>current : c.floor<current) && (c.kind==='dest' || (dir>0?c.kind==='up':c.kind==='down')));\\n  if (ahead.length) choose nearest ahead\\n  else { direction=-direction; choose nearest candidate any; }\\n} else choose nearest candidate any.\\n```\\nIf chosen floor current and state at floor after close: open. But servedThisDoorCycle false after close. For leftover same-floor calls while no passengers, reopen okay.\\nInfer direction for chosen candidate: if floor===current: if kind up -> +1, down -> -1, dest -> keep direction or 0. else sign.\\n\\nAlso at door close we call `_pickNextTarget`; if chosen current floor (e.g., same floor call) state DOOR_OPENING. Good.\\n\\nDuring MOVING re-evaluate:\\n- Only if no pending? still moving with passengers. Each tick, if state MOVING:\\n  - compute candidates matching current direction ahead of carY and <= target? Also destinations ahead. Find closest stop floor > carY (if up) or < carY. If exists and closer than target in direction, set target. Need not consider current floor? carY not integer. Include dests and matching calls. Only change if candidate strictly between current position and target (or if target no longer valid).\\n  - If target no longer needed? maybe.\\n  - Move carY by speed*dt toward target.\\n  - If abs(carY-target)<0.02 -> carY=target; currentFloor=target; state=DOOR_OPENING; doorTimer=0.\\nAlso if direction 0 while moving? shouldn't.\\n\\nDoor open on arrival:\\n```\\n_openDoors() {\\n this.state='DOOR_OPEN'; this.doorTimer=0;\\n this.servedThisDoorCycle=true; this.lastServedFloor=currentFloor;\\n const dir=this.direction;\\n this.destinations.delete(currentFloor);\\n if (dir>0) this.upCalls.delete(currentFloor);\\n else if (dir<0) this.downCalls.delete(currentFloor);\\n else { this.upCalls.delete(currentFloor); this.downCalls.delete(currentFloor); }\\n // If no remaining stops in current direction, clear opposite call at this floor\\n if (!this._hasStopsAhead(dir)) {\\n   if (dir>0) this.downCalls.delete(currentFloor);\\n   if (dir<0) this.upCalls.delete(currentFloor);\\n   if (dir===0) { ... }\\n }\\n}\\n```\\nNote _hasStopsAhead checks strictly ahead and destinations. If none ahead, clear opposite at this floor. Good.\\n\\nPotential: at floor0 up call, direction inferred +1, clears up. no ahead, clears down. fine.\\n\\n`_hasStopsAhead(dir)` returns true if any destination floor ahead or upCalls ahead (dir>0) or downCalls ahead. If dir=0 false.\\n\\nisAcceptingAt: if state DOOR_OPEN current floor. if direction 0 true. if caller dir===this.direction true. else if !_hasStopsAhead(this.direction) true. But if current direction up and no up stops ahead but down call at this floor was cleared at open, a down caller can board (accept) and press dest. Fine.\\n\\nDoor open tick:\\n```\\nif (state DOOR_OPEN) {\\n doorTimer += dt;\\n const pending = pendingBoarders.size + pendingDisembark.size;\\n if (pending===0 && doorTimer>=MIN) {state=DOOR_CLOSING; doorTimer=0;}\\n else if (doorTimer>=MAX) { // force close\\n   // clear pending boarders and disembark? release spots\\n   this.pendingBoarders.forEach((spot,p)=>{if(spotOccupancy[spot.index]===p) spotOccupancy[spot.index]=null;});\\n   this.pendingBoarders.clear();\\n   this.pendingDisembark.clear();\\n   state=DOOR_CLOSING; doorTimer=0;\\n }\\n}\\n```\\nShould we clear pendingDisembark on forced close? If a passenger is mid-exit and not complete, closing leaves them passenger and still in car; maybe not good but safety. Tests only close. We'll clear pendingBoarders only, keep pendingDisembark? If kept, next open might. But safety cap should close even if something never completes. Clear both and leave passengers set? Then passengers stuck but can exit later. Could remove pending disembark from passengers? Hmm. We'll clear pendingDisembark, leave passenger in passengers. That's okay.\\n\\nDoor closing tick: after DOOR_CLOSE_TIME, state='IDLE', servedThisDoorCycle=false; then immediately `_pickNextTarget()` maybe sets MOVING/OPENING. If IDLE and target same floor leftover call, opens. Good. But `servedThisDoorCycle` maybe not needed after reset. Keep.\\n\\nIDLE tick: if calls/dests exist pick. Also if current floor has dest/call and no? pick handles. If no work state IDLE.\\n\\nMOVING tick and re-evaluate: need account door states.\\n\\n`_chooseNearest(list, current)`: choose min abs floor-current; tie prefer dest.\\n\\nOne issue: pick after closing with leftover same floor hall call and no passengers may open again immediately; fine capacity available. But if car full of passengers (passengers>0, dests) chooses dest.\\n\\nDoor opening time and closing time count. Tick dt could be huge 9.6; state transitions one per tick. Door opening takes one tick, then door open next, etc. At 600x this means doors take ~3 frames ~50ms real, okay. Boarders might only have one frame DOOR_OPEN before min elapses? MIN 3 < dt 9.6, but pendingBoarders holds. Good.\\n\\nNeed tick while DOOR_OPENING: if doorTimer>=DOOR_OPEN_TIME -> _openDoors. If dt huge, okay.\\n\\nAlso if state IDLE at floor and calls at current, pick opens.\\n\\nLet's write file with tests later.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-99e707d7235b07bc","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/home/jeff/Code/llm-eval/evals/pi_openrouter_deepseek_deepseek-v4_1-flash-1017_office_prompt_v3/elevator_logic.js","content":"/* elevator_logic.js - pure, deterministic elevator scheduler (no DOM / Three.js). */\n(function (root) {\n    \"use strict\";\n\n    const STATE_IDLE = \"IDLE\";\n    const STATE_MOVING = \"MOVING\";\n    const STATE_OPENING = \"DOOR_OPENING\";\n    const STATE_OPEN = \"DOOR_OPEN\";\n    const STATE_CLOSING = \"DOOR_CLOSING\";\n\n    const MIN_DOOR_OPEN_S = 3.0;\n    const MAX_DOOR_OPEN_S = 18.0;\n    const DOOR_OPEN_TIME = 1.2;\n    const DOOR_CLOSE_TIME = 1.0;\n    const FLOOR_TRAVEL_SPEED = 2.6;\n\n    class ElevatorLogic {\n        constructor(options) {\n            const opts = options || {};\n            this.floorCount = opts.floorCount !== undefined ? opts.floorCount : 6;\n            this.maxCapacity = opts.maxCapacity !== undefined ? opts.maxCapacity : 4;\n            this.floorHeight = opts.floorHeight !== undefined ? opts.floorHeight : 3.4;\n            this.spotCount = Math.min(4, this.maxCapacity);\n            this.minDoorOpenS = opts.minDoorOpenS !== undefined ? opts.minDoorOpenS : MIN_DOOR_OPEN_S;\n            this.maxDoorOpenS = opts.maxDoorOpenS !== undefined ? opts.maxDoorOpenS : MAX_DOOR_OPEN_S;\n            this.doorOpenTime = opts.doorOpenTime !== undefined ? opts.doorOpenTime : DOOR_OPEN_TIME;\n            this.doorCloseTime = opts.doorCloseTime !== undefined ? opts.doorCloseTime : DOOR_CLOSE_TIME;\n            this.travelSpeed = opts.travelSpeed !== undefined ? opts.travelSpeed : FLOOR_TRAVEL_SPEED;\n            this.reset();\n        }\n\n        reset() {\n            this.upCalls = new Set();\n            this.downCalls = new Set();\n            this.destinations = new Set();\n            this.passengers = new Set();\n            this.pendingBoarders = new Map();\n            this.pendingDisembark = new Set();\n            this.spotOccupancy = new Array(this.spotCount).fill(null);\n            this.direction = 0;\n            this.currentFloor = 0;\n            this.targetFloor = 0;\n            this.carY = 0;\n            this.state = STATE_IDLE;\n            this.doorTimer = 0;\n            this.servedThisDoorCycle = false;\n            this.lastServedFloor = -1;\n        }\n\n        callUp(floor) {\n            if (!Number.isFinite(floor)) return;\n            const f = Math.round(floor);\n            if (f < 0 || f >= this.floorCount) return;\n            this.upCalls.add(f);\n        }\n\n        callDown(floor) {\n            if (!Number.isFinite(floor)) return;\n            const f = Math.round(floor);\n            if (f < 0 || f >= this.floorCount) return;\n            this.downCalls.add(f);\n        }\n\n        pressDestination(floor) {\n            if (!Number.isFinite(floor)) return;\n            const f = Math.round(floor);\n            if (f < 0 || f >= this.floorCount) return;\n            this.destinations.add(f);\n        }\n\n        currentCapacityFree() {\n            return this.maxCapacity - (this.passengers.size + this.pendingBoarders.size);\n        }\n\n        reserveBoardingSpot(person) {\n            if (this.currentCapacityFree() <= 0) return null;\n            let freeIndex = -1;\n            for (let i = 0; i < this.spotCount; i += 1) {\n                if (this.spotOccupancy[i] === null || this.spotOccupancy[i] === undefined) {\n                    freeIndex = i;\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n            if (freeIndex < 0) return null;\n            const spots = [\n                { x: -0.58, y: 0, z: 0.56 },\n                { x: 0.58, y: 0, z: 0.56 },\n                { x: -0.58, y: 0, z: -0.56 },\n                { x: 0.58, y: 0, z: -0.56 }\n            ];\n            const base = spots[freeIndex];\n            const spot = { index: freeIndex, x: base.x, y: base.y, z: base.z };\n            this.spotOccupancy[freeIndex] = person;\n            this.pendingBoarders.set(person, spot);\n            return spot;\n        }\n\n        completeBoard(person) {\n            if (this.pendingBoarders.has(person)) {\n                this.pendingBoarders.delete(person);\n                this.passengers.add(person);\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (this.currentCapacityFree() > 0) {\n                this.passengers.add(person);\n                return true;\n            }\n            return false;\n        }\n\n        registerDisembark(person) {\n            if (this.passengers.has(person)) this.pendingDisembark.add(person);\n        }\n\n        completeDisembark(person) {\n            this.passengers.delete(person);\n            this.pendingDisembark.delete(person);\n            for (let i = 0; i < this.spotOccupancy.length; i += 1) {\n                if (this.spotOccupancy[i] === person) this.spotOccupancy[i] = null;\n            }\n        }\n\n        _hasStopsAhead(direction) {\n            if (direction === 0) return false;\n            const current = this.currentFloor;\n            for (const floor of this.destinations) {\n                if (direction > 0 && floor > current) return true;\n                if (direction < 0 && floor < current) return true;\n            }\n            const calls = direction > 0 ? this.upCalls : this.downCalls;\n            for (const floor of calls) {\n                if (direction > 0 && floor > current) return true;\n                if (direction < 0 && floor < current) return true;\n            }\n            return false;\n        }\n\n        isAcceptingAt(floor, direction) {\n            if (this.state !== STATE_OPEN || this.currentFloor !== floor) return false;\n            if (this.direction === 0) return true;\n            if (direction === this.direction) return true;\n            return !this._hasStopsAhead(this.direction);\n        }\n\n        _candidates() {\n            const list = [];\n            for (const floor of this.destinations) {\n                list.push({ floor: floor, kind: \"dest\" });\n            }\n            for (const floor of this.upCalls) {\n                list.push({ floor: floor, kind: \"up\" });\n            }\n            for (const floor of this.downCalls) {\n                list.push({ floor: floor, kind: \"down\" });\n            }\n            return list;\n        }\n\n        _nearest(list, current) {\n            let best = null;\n            let bestDist = Infinity;\n            for (let i = 0; i < list.length; i += 1) {\n                const item = list[i];\n                const dist = Math.abs(item.floor - current);\n                if (dist < bestDist || (dist === bestDist && item.kind === \"dest\" && best && best.kind !== \"dest\")) {\n                    best = item;\n                    bestDist = dist;\n                }\n            }\n            return best;\n        }\n\n        _setTarget(floor, kind) {\n            this.targetFloor = floor;\n            if (floor > this.currentFloor) this.direction = 1;\n            else if (floor < this.currentFloor) this.direction = -1;\n            else if (kind === \"up\") this.direction = 1;\n            else if (kind === \"down\") this.direction = -1;\n\n            if (floor === this.currentFloor) {\n                this.state = STATE_OPENING;\n                this.doorTimer = 0;\n            } else {\n                this.state = STATE_MOVING;\n            }\n        }\n\n        _pickNextTarget() {\n            const current = this.currentFloor;\n            const all = this._candidates();\n            if (!all.length) {\n                this.direction = 0;\n                this.targetFloor = current;\n                this.state = STATE_IDLE;\n                return;\n            }\n\n            const dests = all.filter(function (item) { return item.kind === \"dest\"; });\n\n            // Riders already inside outrank hall calls at the current floor.\n            if (this.passengers.size > 0 && dests.length > 0) {\n                let ahead = dests;\n                if (this.direction > 0) {\n                    ahead = dests.filter(function (item) { return item.floor > current; });\n                } else if (this.direction < 0) {\n                    ahead = dests.filter(function (item) { return item.floor < current; });\n                }\n                if (!ahead.length) ahead = dests;\n                const choice = this._nearest(ahead, current);\n                this._setTarget(choice.floor, \"dest\");\n                return;\n            }\n\n            let pool = all;\n            if (this.direction !== 0) {\n                const dir = this.direction;\n                const ahead = all.filter(function (item) {\n                    if (dir > 0 && item.floor <= current) return false;\n                    if (dir < 0 && item.floor >= current) return false;\n                    if (item.kind === \"dest\") return true;\n                    return dir > 0 ? item.kind === \"up\" : item.kind === \"down\";\n                });\n                if (ahead.length) {\n                    pool = ahead;\n                } else {\n                    this.direction = -this.direction;\n                    pool = all;\n                }\n            }\n\n            const choice = this._nearest(pool, current);\n            if (!choice) {\n                this.direction = 0;\n                this.targetFloor = current;\n                this.state = STATE_IDLE;\n                return;\n            }\n            this._setTarget(choice.floor, choice.kind);\n        }\n\n        _onDoorsOpen() {\n            this.state = STATE_OPEN;\n            this.doorTimer = 0;\n            this.servedThisDoorCycle = true;\n            this.lastServedFloor = this.currentFloor;\n            const floor = this.currentFloor;\n            this.destinations.delete(floor);\n            if (this.direction > 0) {\n                this.upCalls.delete(floor);\n            } else if (this.direction < 0) {\n                this.downCalls.delete(floor);\n            } else {\n                this.upCalls.delete(floor);\n                this.downCalls.delete(floor);\n            }\n            if (!this._hasStopsAhead(this.direction)) {\n                if (this.direction > 0) this.downCalls.delete(floor);\n                else if (this.direction < 0) this.upCalls.delete(floor);\n                else {\n                    this.upCalls.delete(floor);\n                    this.downCalls.delete(floor);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        _reconsiderWhileMoving() {\n            if (this.state !== STATE_MOVING) return;\n            const dir = this.direction;\n            if (dir === 0) return;\n            const y = this.carY;\n            let bestFloor = this.targetFloor;\n            let bestDist = Math.abs(this.targetFloor - y);\n            const consider = (floor) => {\n                if (dir > 0 && floor <= y) return;\n                if (dir < 0 && floor >= y) return;\n                const dist = Math.abs(floor - y);\n                if (dist < bestDist - 1e-6) {\n                    bestDist = dist;\n                    bestFloor = floor;\n                }\n            };\n            for (const floor of this.destinations) consider(floor);\n            const calls = dir > 0 ? this.upCalls : this.downCalls;\n            for (const floor of calls) consider(floor);\n            if (bestFloor !== this.targetFloor) this.targetFloor = bestFloor;\n        }\n\n        tick(dt) {\n            const step = Math.max(0, Number(dt) || 0);\n            if (this.state === STATE_IDLE) {\n                this._pickNextTarget();\n                return;\n            }\n\n            if (this.state === STATE_OPENING) {\n                this.doorTimer += step;\n                if (this.doorTimer >= this.doorOpenTime) this._onDoorsOpen();\n                return;\n    