LED<->AWAY based on id. But GONE? Could set DISABLED for GONE too, removing group. Active left. For id<target, DISABLED->AWAY. We'll implement:\\n```\\nif enabled && state==='DISABLED' state='AWAY';\\nif !enabled && (state==='AWAY') state='DISABLED';\\nif !enabled && state==='GONE' { state='DISABLED'; hide; }\\n```\\nBut if active id>= target leave. On next day reset uses target. Also topUp should skip disabled.\\n\\n`countPresent`: state not DISABLED/AWAY/GONE. Include ARRIVING etc.\\n\\n`topUpVisitors`:\\n```\\nconst minute=simClock.simMinute;\\nif (minute<480 || minute>1080) return; // 8:00..18:00\\nlet deficit = targetOccupancy - countPresent();\\nif deficit<=0 return;\\nfor each visitor state AWAY or GONE and id<targetOccupancy:\\n  rearm: state='AWAY'; arrivalTime = minute + randInt(0,6); visitDuration=randInt(30,100); departureTime=...; group.visible=false; if parent remove? if GONE removed; plan=[]; currentAction=null; reservedSeats release; deficit--; if 0 break\\n```\\nBut if visitor is GONE and we rearm, group already removed; spawn later adds. If AWAY disabled no. Ensure visitor id < targetOccupancy (enabled). Also if state DISABLED skip. If state AWAY but currently arrivalTime far future due initial 8:00-10:00 and deficit >0, topup may rearm them sooner. That's okay, but could rearm the same visitor every frame if deficit remains and it's AWAY with arrival now+6, because loop picks it again next frame, resetting arrivalTime always now+6 => never arrives! Need avoid rearming an AWAY visitor that is already scheduled soon. Only rearm if state==='GONE' OR (state==='AWAY' && (arrivalTime===null || arrivalTime - now > 12?))? Initial visitor arrival far future maybe. But to keep population, choose only GONE first. If not enough, rearm AWAY with arrivalTime > now+10 maybe. Let's implement:\\n```\\nif visitor.state==='GONE' -> rearm\\nelse if visitor.state==='AWAY' && visitor.arrivalTime > now + 15 -> rearm\\n```\\nBut after rearm arrival now+0..6, next frame arrivalTime > now+15 false, so not rearmed again. Good. If arrival <= now spawn immediately next frame. Good.\\nAlso if visitor state GONE and target not reached, rearm. Break when deficit satisfied.\\nNeed not rearm workers.\\n\\nSpawn logic each frame:\\n```\\nfor agent:\\n if DISABLED skip\\n if state AWAY and id<targetOccupancy and simMinute>=arrivalTime and simMinute< maybe departureTime+?:\\n   if role VISITOR and simMinute>1080? maybe no spawn\\n   spawnAgent(agent)\\n```\\nWorkers: if simMinute>=arrivalTime and < departureTime? If simMinute > departureTime, skip (don't spawn late). But if simMinute after midnight reset etc. Use if now < departureTime + 30 maybe. If missed day, don't spawn. If now>=arrival && now<=departure. For visitors now between 8 and 18.\\nSpawn:\\n- group visible true; if parent not scene, scene.add(group) (if parent car? detach scene.attach).\\n- set position outside with jitter x ±1.1 z ±0.75, y=0.\\n- state ARRIVING; floor=0; leaving=false; hasLunched=false for workers (already from schedule); plan = role worker ? planArriveToDesk(agent) : planVisitorVisit(agent); currentAction=null; path=[].\\n- isSitting false; isWalking false; group.rotation.y = Math.PI? Facing building (-Z) default nose +Z, walking from outside z12 into building decreasing z -> facing -Z -> rotation.y=Math.PI. Our walking function can orient toward movement direction. We'll update rotation.y during walk.\\n\\nWalking orientation: In walkAlongPath, compute dx,dz; desired facing = atan2(dx,dz) because nose +Z; rotation.y = atan2(dx,dz). For moving -Z dx=0 dz=-1 -> atan2(0,-1)=PI. Good. Set agent.group.rotation.y = desired. For seated orientation set by SIT.\\n\\nBut rotation.y also used for sitting; when walking then sit. Good.\\n\\nAction dispatch:\\n`processAgent(agent, motionDt)`:\\n- schedule spawn handled outside.\\n- maybe departure override for workers.\\n- if state GONE/DISABLED/AWAY skip.\\n- loop up to 16:\\n  - if !currentAction: if plan.length shift; else chooseNextActivity(agent) maybe. Need avoid choose if leaving/GONE. For plan empty, call chooseNextActivity.\\n  - if currentAction and processAction returns true -> currentAction=null; continue; else break.\\n- animate walking after? We'll call animatePersonWalking globally after collisions.\\n\\nMaybe action processing can call chooseNextActivity which sets plan. Fine.\\n\\nNeed handle `PICK_NEXT_ACTIVITY` maybe redundant. But implement.\\n\\n`startAction(agent, action)`:\\nswitch:\\n- WALK_TO_WP: build path.\\n- WAIT_AT_PANEL: state WAITING_ELEVATOR; press call; action._dir; action._toFloor; maybe.\\n- ENTER_ELEVATOR: action.phase='reserve'; action.spot=null; agent.state WAITING? maybe 'IN_CAR' only after.\\n- EXIT_ELEVATOR: registerDisembark, scene.attach, set y, state ON_FLOOR; action._done=false; action._target = elevWait pos.\\n- SIT: snap.\\n- STAND: ...\\n- RELEASE_SEAT...\\n- WAIT_SIM: untilMin.\\n- EXIT_BUILDING...\\n- PRESS_FLOOR...\\n- WAIT_FOR_FLOOR...\\n- ENTER_STATE...\\n- MARK_LUNCHED...\\n- PICK_NEXT_ACTIVITY...\\nSet action._started=true.\\n\\n`processAction(agent, action, dt)` returns bool done.\\n\\nNeed distinguish zero-duration actions: startAction may complete and return true? We can have processAction call startAction then switch. For SIT etc return true immediately.\\n\\nWALK_TO_WP path building:\\n```\\nfunction buildWalkPath(agent, floor, wpName) {\\n const floorData=world.floors[floor];\\n if (!floorData) return [];\\n const startName=world.nearestNode(floorData.nodes, agent.group.position);\\n const path=world.bfsPath(floorData.nodes,startName,wpName);\\n if (!path.length) { return [floorData.nodes[wpName].pos.clone()]; }\\n // remove first if close to current? We'll set pathIndex 0 but if first pos distance <0.2 skip.\\n agent.path=path; agent.pathIndex=0;\\n // If first node is startName and near, skip\\n if (path.length>1 && path[0].distanceTo(agent.group.position)<0.5) agent.pathIndex=1;\\n agent._prevWp=agent.pathIndex; agent._stallT=0; agent._prevPos = agent.group.position.clone();\\n}\\n```\\nPath positions have y=floor*FH. In walk loop only x/z. If agent group parent scene. We'll set y target floor height on walk start maybe.\\nMovement:\\n```\\nfunction walkAlongPath(agent, dt) {\\n let budget = AGENT_WALK_SPEED * dt;\\n let guard=0;\\n while (budget>0 && agent.pathIndex < agent.path.length && guard<32) {\\n   const target = agent.path[agent.pathIndex];\\n   const pos = agent.group.position;\\n   const dx=target.x-pos.x, dz=target.z-pos.z;\\n   const dist=Math.hypot(dx,dz);\\n   if (dist < 0.12) { agent.pathIndex++; continue; }\\n   const step=Math.min(dist,budget);\\n   pos.x += dx/dist*step; pos.z += dz/dist*step;\\n   // keep y at floor height\\n   pos.y = agent.floor * FH;\\n   agent.group.rotation.y = Math.atan2(dx,dz);\\n   budget-=step;\\n   guard++;\\n }\\n if (agent.pathIndex >= agent.path.length) return true;\\n // stall detection using motion time\\n const prev=agent._prevPos || agent.group.position.clone();\\n const moved=agent.group.position.distanceTo(prev);\\n agent._stallT = (agent._stallT||0) + dt;\\n if (moved < 0.005) {\\n   if (agent._stallT > 1.2) {\\n     // skip waypoint or force advance\\n     agent.pathIndex++;\\n     agent._stallT=0;\\n     // if near entrance threshold, teleport to next waypoint\\n   }\\n } else { agent._stallT=0; }\\n agent._prevPos=agent.group.position.clone();\\n return false;\\n}\\n```\\nBut dt could huge; moved large. Stall detection at low speed. At high dt budget huge, no stall. Fine.\\n\\nEntrance chain stall recovery: if near z>8.5 and stall >1.5, advance to next waypoint by setting pos to target? We'll in stall block if agent.floor===0 && agent.group.position.z>8.3 && action.wp in entrance chain, set position to next path node x,z. But we already increment pathIndex; maybe teleport to that node. Use:\\n```\\nif (agent.currentAction && agent.currentAction.type==='WALK_TO_WP' && agent.currentAction.wp==='front_door_threshold' && stall) { pos.copy(next.pos) }\\n```\\nSimpler: if stalled, agent.pathIndex++ and if next exists set pos.x/z to next. This is \\\"advance it to next entrance waypoint.\\\" But could teleport through walls for any walk. Limit to entrance chain. We'll implement helper isEntranceWp.\\n\\nAlso collision exemption for entrance chain: in applyCollisions skip if action.type WALK_TO_WP and ['outside','front_door_threshold','entrance','lobby_center'].indexOf(action.wp)!==-1.\\n\\nWAIT_AT_PANEL:\\nstart: dir action.dir (or sign toFloor-floor), press.\\nprocess:\\n```\\nif (elevator.state==='DOOR_OPEN' && elevator.currentFloor===floor && elevator.isAcceptingAt(floor,dir) && elevator.currentCapacityFree()>0) return true;\\n// re-press every frame if missing\\nif (dir>0) elevator.callUp(floor); else elevator.callDown(floor);\\nagent.state='WAITING_ELEVATOR';\\nreturn false;\\n```\\nNeed if current floor 0 and dir down? shouldn't. If floor top and up? no. \\nMaybe if car at floor but full, keep waiting. Press call again.\\n\\nENTER_ELEVATOR:\\nWe need know agent.floor and action.toFloor. Start phase reserve. process:\\n```\\nconst dir = action.toFloor>agent.floor?1:-1;\\nif (action.phase==='reserve') {\\n  if (!action.spot) {\\n    if (elevator.isAcceptingAt(agent.floor,dir) && elevator.currentCapacityFree()>0) {\\n      action.spot=elevator.reserveBoardingSpot(agent);\\n      if (!action.spot) { press; return false; }\\n      action.phase='door';\\n      action._prevWalk = agent.group.position.clone(); action._stallT=0;\\n    } else { press call; return false; }\\n  } else { action.phase='door'; }\\n}\\nif (action.phase==='door') {\\n  const targetX = action.spot.x; // world x same as car x\\n  const targetZ = 1.45; // just in front of doors\\n  // direct move toward (targetX, floorY, targetZ)\\n  const pos=agent.group.position; dx=targetX-pos.x; dz=targetZ-pos.z; dist=Math.hypot\\n  const step=AGENT_WALK_SPEED*dt;\\n  if (dist<=0.3 || step>=dist) { pos.x=targetX; pos.z=targetZ; action.phase='inside'; }\\n  else { pos.x += dx/dist*step; pos.z += dz/dist*step; pos.y=floor*FH; rotation.y=atan2(dx,dz);}\\n  // stall: if no progress 1.5 motion sec, teleport threshold\\n  ...\\n  return false;\\n}\\nif (action.phase==='inside') {\\n  elevator.carGroup.attach(agent.group);\\n  agent.state='IN_CAR';\\n  action.phase='spot';\\n  // after attach, group local pos should be near door\\n}\\nif (action.phase==='spot') {\\n  const localTarget = new THREE.Vector3(action.spot.x, 0, action.spot.z);\\n  const pos=agent.group.position; dx=localTarget.x-pos.x; dz=localTarget.z-pos.z; dist...\\n  step=AGENT_WALK_SPEED*dt;\\n  if (dist<=0.08 || step>=dist) { pos.copy(localTarget); elevator.completeBoard(agent); agent.group.rotation.y=0; return true; }\\n  else move...\\n  return false;\\n}\\n```\\nNeed doors hold for pendingBoarders. We reserve then walk. Good.\\nBut if car moves while boarder walking? Logic holds pending. Car stays. Good.\\nIf car is not at floor (slipped away) after reservation? We check isAccepting before reserve. Could car start closing while pending? No, pending prevents closing. If max door timer force closes, pending cleared, boarder may still be walking; then car may leave. Our action phase door should re-check if state not open at floor; then release spot? There's no release method. Could call completeBoard? Hmm. Edge. We can if car leaves and phase door and not at floor, reset action.spot? But spotOccupancy stuck. Add logic method releaseBoardingSpot? Not specified. We can avoid by reservation only when open and then car holds. Safety cap 18 sim sec might force if at 600x walk takes <1 frame, so no. Fine.\\n\\nNeed walking collision exemption for ENTER_ELEVATOR in applyCollisions.\\n\\nPRESS_FLOOR: press destination action.floor; maybe set state IN_CAR. complete.\\nWAIT_FOR_FLOOR: if elevator.state==='DOOR_OPEN' && currentFloor===action.floor return true. Also if state maybe door closing? no. agent state IN_CAR. Maybe if not in car? no.\\nEXIT_ELEVATOR:\\nstart: elevator.registerDisembark(agent); scene.attach(agent.group); agent.floor=action.toFloor; agent.group.position.y=agent.floor*FH; agent.state='ON_FLOOR'; action._target = elevWait pos. Maybe set path direct [target]. Use direct movement rather than BFS because position inside car. `action._exitTarget=world.floors[toFloor].nodes.elevWait.pos.clone()`. \\nprocess: move toward target direct at speed. Need doors held. If dist<=0.2 completeDisembark and return true. Stall recovery after 1.5 -> teleport target. Exempt collision.\\nPotential: scene.attach preserves world pos at car y. We set y floor*FH. good.\\nCould agent get pushed? collision skip EXIT.\\n\\nSIT:\\nstart:\\n```\\nconst floorData=world.floors[action.floor]; const node=floorData.nodes[action.wp]; const target=floorData.sitTargets[action.wp]||{sit:false,facing:0};\\nconst pos = node.pos.clone();\\nif (!target.sit) { jitter radius .35-.75; }\\nagent.group.position.set(pos.x+jx, action.floor*FH, pos.z+jz);\\nagent.group.rotation.y=target.facing;\\nagent.group.userData.isSitting=!!target.sit;\\nagent.group.userData.isWalking=false;\\nif (target.sit) agent.group.position.y=action.floor*FH-0.35;\\nagent.floor=action.floor;\\n```\\nNeed \\\"legs directed toward desk away from backrest\\\": facing set correctly. For standing no sit.\\nReturn true.\\nCould reserve seat at plan compile; no action.\\nSTAND:\\n```\\nagent.group.userData.isSitting=false; agent.group.userData.isWalking=false;\\nif (agent.group.parent===elevator.carGroup) y=0 else y=agent.floor*FH;\\nagent.group.position.y=y;\\n```\\nReturn true.\\nRELEASE_SEAT: if action.seatKey release; else releaseAgentSeats(agent); complete.\\nWAIT_SIM: if !untilMin set = simClock.simMinute + (action.minutes||0); if simMinute>=untilMin return true else false.\\nEXIT_BUILDING: releaseAgentSeats; if parent remove; visible false; state GONE; leaving=false; return true. For worker maybe arrivalTime next day.\\nENTER_STATE: agent.state=action.state; return true.\\nMARK_LUNCHED: agent.hasLunched=true; return true.\\nPICK_NEXT_ACTIVITY: chooseNextActivity(agent); return true. But if choose sets plan and currentAction still this; after returning true currentAction=null and loop continues to plan. Good.\\n\\n`chooseNextActivity(agent)`:\\n- if worker and simMinute>=departureTime -> agent.plan=planLeaveBuilding(agent); return.\\n- meetings: find index where simMinute>=time && simMinute-time<90. remove splice. planAttendMeeting.\\n- lunch: if simMinute>=lunchTime && !hasLunched && simMinute<15*60 -> planGoToLunch.\\n- random r. if r<0.14 planAttendMeeting; else if <0.26 planVisitLounge; else if <0.41 planVisitCoworker; else planWorkAtDesk.\\n- visitor? If choose called for visitor unexpectedly, planVisitorVisit? But visitor plans end with exit, no PICK. Could fallback planLeaveBuilding.\\nNeed avoid recursive planAttendMeeting fallback to planVisitLounge. Fine.\\n\\n`planWorkAtDesk(agent)`:\\nIf not at desk maybe travel? Usually at desk after previous. We can create actions:\\n- if agent.state==='AT_DESK' && group sitting: [WAIT_SIM(randInt(18,65)), PICK_NEXT_ACTIVITY]. But if not at desk, go home.\\nWe'll implement generic `planReturnToDesk(agent)` for after activities. For work, if current floor === homeFloor and state AT_DESK: wait+pick. Else build return to desk actions with SIT, ENTER_STATE, WAIT, PICK.\\nWe need ensure if agent sitting in desk, WAIT only. `makeWorkTail(agent, minutes)` maybe.\\n\\nPlan helpers:\\n\\n`appendTravel(actions, agent, fromFloor, toFloor)`:\\n```\\nif (fromFloor===toFloor) return;\\nconst dir=toFloor>fromFloor?1:-1;\\nactions.push({type:'WALK_TO_WP',floor:fromFloor,wp:'elevWait'});\\nactions.push({type:'WAIT_AT_PANEL',floor:fromFloor,dir:dir,toFloor:toFloor});\\nactions.push({type:'ENTER_ELEVATOR',toFloor:toFloor,floor:fromFloor});\\nactions.push({type:'PRESS_FLOOR',floor:toFloor});\\nactions.push({type:'WAIT_FOR_FLOOR',floor:toFloor});\\nactions.push({type:'EXIT_ELEVATOR',toFloor:toFloor,floor:toFloor});\\n```\\nBut fromFloor for ENTER should be agent.floor, which is fromFloor. EXIT sets floor to toFloor. Good.\\n\\n`planArriveToDesk(agent)`:\\n```\\n[\\n {WALK outside}, {WALK threshold}, {WALK entrance}, {WALK lobby_center},\\n {WALK elevWait}, WAIT_AT_PANEL(0,1,home), ENTER(home), PRESS(home), WAIT_FOR(home), EXIT(home),\\n WALK homeFloor deskDoor, WALK desk, ENTER_STATE AT_DESK, SIT(desk),\\n WAIT_SIM(randInt(20,55)), PICK\\n]\\n```\\nNeed after EXIT floor set home. Good.\\n\\n`planLeaveBuilding(agent)`:\\nUse current floor agent.floor. If sitting -> STAND. RELEASE_SEAT maybe. WALK_TO_WP(floor,'elevWait') maybe from desk. Then travel down to 0. Then walk lobby_center, entrance, threshold, outside, EXIT_BUILDING. For visitors same. Set leaving=true. If agent.floor 0 skip travel; still walk.\\n```\\nactions=[{STAND},{RELEASE_SEAT}, {WALK_TO_WP floor elevWait}]\\nappendTravel(actions,agent,floor,0)\\nactions.push WALK lobby_center, entrance, threshold, outside, EXIT_BUILDING\\n```\\nBut if agent is at elevator wait already and floor maybe current, BFS fine. If agent floor0 and not at desk, walk to elevWait maybe unnecessary but okay then to lobby. Could use lobby_center directly. For floor0, use WALK lobby_center.\\nSet agent.leaving=true.\\nPotential when agent currently IN_CAR: planLeaveBuilding not called. Good.\\n\\n`planGoToLunch`:\\n```\\nactions=[STAND, RELEASE_SEAT, WALK elevWait]\\nappendTravel(actions,agent,agent.floor,0)\\nchoose bistro seat free reserveSeat; if none use cafe_order stand.\\nif seat: WALK bistro, ENTER_STATE AT_LUNCH, SIT, WAIT lunchDuration, STAND, RELEASE_SEAT\\nelse WALK cafe_order, ENTER_STATE AT_LUNCH, WAIT lunchDuration\\nMARK_LUNCHED\\nWALK elevWait\\nappendTravel(0,homeFloor)\\nWALK deskDoor? direct desk\\nWALK desk, ENTER_STATE AT_DESK, SIT, WAIT_SIM(randInt(20,45)), PICK\\n```\\nNeed after SIT bistro then STAND then RELEASE. Note seat reservation at compile. If all seats taken, fallback to cafe_order stand. Good.\\n`agent.floor` at compile from current. fine.\\n\\n`planVisitLounge`:\\n```\\nconst floor=agent.floor; choose free lounge spot from floorData.loungeSpots using reserveSeat; if none use water_cooler stand.\\nactions=[STAND, RELEASE_SEAT, WALK_TO_WP(floor, spot/water)]\\nif sit: ENTER_STATE AT_BREAK, SIT, WAIT 5..12, STAND, RELEASE_SEAT\\nelse ENTER_STATE AT_BREAK, WAIT 5..12\\nthen return desk: WALK desk, ENTER_STATE AT_DESK, SIT, WAIT 15..40, PICK\\n```\\nFrom lounge to desk BFS via nearest. Good.\\nIf agent already at break? no.\\n\\n`planAttendMeeting`:\\n- target floor 65% home else randInt 1..5.\\n- get conf seats; find free using reserveSeat. If none fallback planVisitLounge (but ensure agent maybe not at desk? choose called at desk mostly). Return planVisitLounge.\\n- actions=[STAND, RELEASE_SEAT, WALK elevWait] (if agent.floor same target, still walk to conf)\\n- appendTravel(agent.floor,target)\\n- WALK conf_center maybe then seat. Use WALK_TO_WP(target,'conf_center'), WALK seat.\\n- ENTER_STATE IN_MEETING, SIT(seat), WAIT 22..45, STAND, RELEASE_SEAT\\n- Return: WALK elevWait, appendTravel(target,homeFloor), WALK desk, ENTER_STATE AT_DESK, SIT desk, WAIT randInt(20,50), PICK.\\nIf target===home floor, appendTravel skips.\\nReserve seat at compile.\\nNeed if all seats reserved fallback lounge. But planVisitLounge will reserve a lounge seat. Fine.\\n\\n`planVisitCoworker`:\\n- candidates agents role worker, state AT_DESK, id != agent.id. pick random.\\n- targetFloor=other.homeFloor; targetDoor=other.deskDoorWpName.\\n- actions=[STAND, RELEASE_SEAT, WALK elevWait]\\n- appendTravel(agent.floor,targetFloor)\\n- WALK_TO_WP(targetFloor,targetDoor), ENTER_STATE VISITING, WAIT 6..18\\n- WALK elevWait, appendTravel(targetFloor,agent.homeFloor), WALK desk, ENTER_STATE AT_DESK, SIT desk, WAIT randInt(20,45), PICK.\\nIf no candidate -> planWorkAtDesk. But planWorkAtDesk if at desk returns wait.\\n\\n`planReturnToDesk(agent, minutes)`:\\nCould be used after meeting/lunch/lounge. But we wrote inline.\\n\\nVisitor plan:\\n```\\nfunction planVisitorVisit(agent) {\\n const actions=[];\\n actions.push WALK outside, threshold, entrance, lobby_center;\\n const roll=Math.random();\\n let activity;\\n if roll<0.10 bistro\\n else if <0.16 cafe counter\\n else if <0.30 front lounge\\n else if <0.42 back/pit\\n else if <0.52 stand spot\\n else if <0.62 loiter\\n else if <0.77 office floor lounge\\n else meeting\\n ...\\n then exit chain.\\n}\\n```\\nNeed if agent spawns at outside; yes.\\nFor bistro: reserve seat floor0 bistro; if none fallback loiter. Walk seat, ENTER_STATE VISITING/AT_LUNCH? Use 'VISITING'. SIT, WAIT 15..35, STAND, RELEASE.\\ncafe counter: WALK cafe_order, ENTER_STATE VISITING, WAIT 5..12.\\nfront lounge: reserve front_lounge spot; if none stand. WALK, SIT, wait.\\nback/pit: reserve from backSpots; WALK, SIT, wait.\\nstand spot: choose floor0 standSpots (cafe_order etc) or lobby_wc. WALK, ENTER_STATE VISITING, WAIT 5..15.\\nloiter: choose loiterSpots, WALK, WAIT 8..20.\\noffice lounge: choose floor 1..5, choose free lounge spot on that floor; if none stand water_cooler. actions WALK elevWait, appendTravel(0,floor), WALK spot, SIT if seat, WAIT 10..25, STAND, RELEASE, WALK elevWait, appendTravel(floor,0).\\nmeeting: choose floor 1..5, reserve conf seat; if none fallback lobby loiter (need not reserve). If seat: travel up, walk conf_center, seat, ENTER_STATE IN_MEETING, SIT, WAIT 20..40, STAND, RELEASE, travel down.\\nThen exit: WALK lobby_center, entrance, threshold, outside, EXIT_BUILDING.\\nBut after office activity agent floor 0. Good. After bistro etc floor 0. Good.\\nIf meeting on floor and all seats taken -> fallback loiter at lobby (no travel). Implement function maybe.\\nNeed ensure reservation released if fallback after reserve? We only reserve if seat available. Good.\\n\\n`reserveSeat(agent, floor, wp)`:\\n```\\nconst key=floor+':'+wp;\\nif (seatReservations.has(key)) return null;\\nseatReservations.add(key);\\nagent.reservedSeats.push(key);\\nreturn key;\\n```\\n`releaseSeat(agent,key)` remove.\\n`releaseAgentSeats(agent)`.\\n\\nSeat reservation for bistro floor0 etc.\\n\\n`randomChoice`.\\n\\n`appendExit` helper.\\n\\nPotential issue: Worker desk seats not reserved, but visitors don't go to desks. Fine.\\n\\nDaily schedule:\\n`maybeDepart(agent)` in frame:\\n```\\nif agent.role==='WORKER' && !agent.leaving && agent.state not in AWAY,DISABLED,GONE,IN_CAR,WAITING_ELEVATOR,ARRIVING,LEAVING? and simMinute>=departureTime:\\n if agent.currentAction && (ENTER/WAIT_FOR/EXIT/WAIT_AT_PANEL) return; // finish elevator\\n agent.leaving=true; releaseAgentSeats(agent); agent.plan=planLeaveBuilding(agent); agent.currentAction=null;\\n```\\nBut if agent is sitting in meeting, planLeaveBuilding starts STAND. If currentAction is SIT zero-duration already done. Good.\\nIf agent is WALKING to somewhere, overriding plan is okay; new plan from current position. Need release seats. If currentAction type WALK_TO_WP, setting null and new plan. Good.\\nIf currentAction type WAIT_SIM, override. If WAIT_AT_PANEL/ENTER/WAIT_FOR/EXIT, let finish; but after exit state ON_FLOOR then next frame override. Need condition:\\n```\\nconst elevatorBusy = ['WAIT_AT_PANEL','ENTER_ELEVATOR','PRESS_FLOOR','WAIT_FOR_FLOOR','EXIT_ELEVATOR'].includes(type)\\nif (!elevatorBusy && agent.state!=='IN_CAR') override.\\n```\\nAlso if state ARRIVING and departure passed? leave anyway.\\nSet agent.leaving=false on GONE.\\n\\nAfter worker reaches GONE, state GONE. On next day reset.\\n\\n`processAgent` should maybe spawn. We'll separate `updateAgents(motionDt)`:\\n```\\nfor agent of agents:\\n if agent.state==='DISABLED' continue;\\n if agent.state==='AWAY' { maybeSpawn(agent); continue; }\\n if agent.state==='GONE' continue;\\n maybeDepart(agent);\\n dispatchActions(agent,motionDt);\\n```\\nBut if agent state AWAY and arrivalTime due spawn. Good.\\n\\n`maybeSpawn` for visitors: ensure id<targetOccupancy, now>=arrivalTime,