ooking at building center: OrbitControls target default 0,0,0. Add target set maybe (0,6,0). Spec camera looking at building center; set controls.target.set(0,6,0). camera.lookAt maybe controls handles.\\n\\nRenderer set pixel ratio maybe not necessary.\\n\\nAnimate:\\n```\\nlet lastTime=0;\\nfunction animate() {\\n requestAnimationFrame(animate);\\n const now=performance.now();\\n const realDt=Math.min(0.05, lastTime? (now-lastTime)/1000 : 0.016);\\n lastTime=now;\\n simClock.tick(realDt);\\n updateLighting();\\n const motionDt=realDt*simClock.timeScale;\\n elevator.tick(motionDt);\\n updateAgents(motionDt);\\n topUpVisitors();\\n applyCollisions();\\n for agents if parent animatePersonWalking(group,motionDt);\\n controls.update();\\n renderer.render(scene,camera);\\n updateHUD();\\n}\\n```\\nNeed topUp after updateAgents maybe before? topup can rearm. Spawn next frame. fine.\\nAt 600x motionDt=0.05*600=30 sim sec/frame. Walk budget 1.35*30=40m per frame; agents cross building instantly, action loops. Elevator tick dt=30 sim sec: doors open/close in one tick each, car moves 78 floors/tick? travelSpeed 2.6*30=78 floors, instantly. This means at max speed elevator teleports and doors cycles in few frames; pending holds. Fine. But potential actions may not catch door open because tick transitions OPENING->OPEN in one tick then next frame OPEN maybe closes immediately due min elapsed and no pending. At max, waiting agents check each frame after elevator.tick. Frame sequence:\\n- elevator.tick: state maybe MOVING -> arrival -> DOOR_OPENING (returns). Waiting not accepted.\\n- next frame: elevator.tick OPENING->OPEN (returns, state OPEN). Then agent WAIT_AT_PANEL sees open and accepts, next action ENTER starts reserve/walk maybe within same frame dispatch. It reserves, car state remains OPEN. Good. Next frame elevator.tick sees pendingBoarders>0, so holds. Agent boards within action loop (walk budget huge) completeBoard. Good. Then pending empty, but elevator.tick already ran this frame before agent completed; next frame closes. Good. Works.\\n\\nBut if there are no waiting agents and doors open, next frame closes. Fine.\\n\\nAt max, timeScale 600 and realDt cap .05 means sim advances max 30 sec/frame. 5.5s runtime ~ maybe 110 frames -> 55 sim min? Actually at 600x with 60fps realDt .016 => 9.6 sim sec/frame * 300 frames = 2880 sim sec=48 min. The runtime check 5.5s only sees morning. But fine. Day wrap not tested. Our reset still works.\\n\\nAt default 120x, day ~ 5.5 real min.\\n\\nPotential action dispatch with motionDt huge: WAIT_SIM sets untilMin and returns false; next frames. Good.\\n\\nCollision apply O(n^2). For 100 agents fine. But agents in AWAY not in scene; skip if !group.parent? We'll skip if !group.visible. Use parent checks.\\n\\n`applyCollisions`:\\n```\\nfor i.. for j..:\\n a=agents[i], b=...\\n if !a.group.parent || !b.group.parent || a.group.parent!==b.group.parent continue;\\n if a.group.parent===elevator.carGroup continue; // skip car all\\n if a.group.userData.isSitting || b... continue;\\n if exempt(a)||exempt(b) continue;\\n const dx=..., dz=..., dy=...\\n if abs(dy)>1.2 continue;\\n const d2=dx*dx+dz*dz;\\n const minDist=0.72; if d2<minDist^2:\\n  let d=sqrt; if d<1e-3 { angle=Math.random()*2pi; nx=cos; nz=sin; d=0; } else ...\\n  const push=(minDist-d)*0.18; // maybe small\\n  a.pos.x -= nx*push; b.pos.x += nx*push etc.\\n```\\nSpec low push scalar 0.18. With d=0 push .13 each. Exact overlap random. Good. Maybe use minDist=0.8. PERSON_R .4 -> .8. We'll use 0.78.\\nAlso maybe clamp y unaffected.\\nNeed skip disabled/away. visible check.\\n\\n`exemptFromCollision(agent)`:\\n- currentAction type ENTER_ELEVATOR or EXIT_ELEVATOR.\\n- WALK_TO_WP and wp in entrance chain.\\n- maybe WAIT_AT_PANEL? no.\\n- if parent car skip anyway.\\n\\nEntrance stall recovery in walk.\\n\\nNeed no unresolved refs. We'll write carefully.\\n\\nStatic checker may flag function parameters in callbacks? We use function(name) etc.\\n\