e if no pending. Waiting agents accept and enter within same frame? Sequence: frame N elevator.tick arrives OPENING; agent WAIT not accepted. Frame N+1 elevator.tick OPENING->OPEN; agent WAIT_AT_PANEL sees open and capacity free -> completes; next action ENTER starts reserve, phase door, moves huge step to threshold and phase inside, attaches, phase spot, moves huge, completeBoard. So boards in same frame. Great. But only up to 4. Then next frame elevator.tick sees pending empty (all complete) and doorTimer already? doorTimer at open was 0, then frame N+1 after elevator.tick state open timer 0. Agent boards. Frame N+2 elevator.tick doorTimer +=10 > min, pending 0 -> CLOSING. So car leaves. Good. So one floor per 3 frames per direction. At 600x, 3 frames=0.05s real, sim 30 sec. Should serve.\n\nBut maybe agents waiting for elevator are not at the car floor because their current action WAIT_AT_PANEL is stuck due direction mismatch and the car never comes to their floor in the matching direction. E.g., visitor at floor5 wants down, but car serves down calls only when direction down. It should. Yet call sets.\n\nCould be a more subtle bug: `WAIT_AT_PANEL` is pressed with dir based on toFloor, but action.floor may not equal agent.floor? In appendTravel, fromFloor is agent.floor at plan compile. If the agent's plan was compiled while in car or floor mismatch, maybe wrong. For planAttendMeeting: appendTravel(agent.floor,target). Agent.floor should be current. For planLeaveBuilding maybe. But wait counts huge.\n\nMaybe visitors top-up keeps spawning new visitors and their plans use upper floors; but 42 waiting is still too many.\n\nLet's inspect actual agent states/actions. Our sim variables are inside IIFE, not exposed. Could temporarily expose `window.__officeDebug = {agents, elevator, world, simClock}` for probing, then remove or keep harmless? It would help. We can add at end startSimulation `window.__officeDebug = ...`. Not forbidden. But final artifact maybe okay. Cou