visitors keep going up/down for office activities, plus workers. Still queue should drain.\n\nMaybe there is a serious starvation due to hall call clearing rules. Notice up call 0 persists. Car at floor4 direction up, down calls 4,2,1. It will go to5 (dest), then reverse down, serve 4,2,1, then at 0? Up0 remains. It may serve down 1 then go to0? There is no down0 call; down call at floor1 cleared at open, but after floor1 it continues down to floor0 because direction down with no more down calls ahead? At door close at floor1, direction down, ahead none, reverse up, pool all: up0 and down? none -> target0 (up call) which is below current? Wait current1, direction reversed up (+1); pool all includes up0 at floor0 below, _nearest chooses 0, _setTarget floor0 (<current) sets direction -1 and MOVING down to0. Good. Then opens at0 (direction down), clears downCalls floor0 none, then if no stops ahead down (none), clears up0 because opposite. Good, up0 cleared! Then riders board? Direction is down but isAcceptingAt(0,+1): hasStopsAhead(down) false, so accepts up callers. They board, press upper. After close, pick passengers dest above -> up. Good. So up0 should clear at open. But debug shows up0 present while car at floor4, because it was re-pressed by waiting agents each frame after clearing. That's fine.\n\nBut why waiting 29? At t=45s (12:52) maybe lunch rush just started and visitor cycle. Still, some workers waiting since lunchTime maybe 11:30 (82 min) at 600x =8s real. Should have been served. Could there be starvation because car repeatedly serves up destinations/calls while down calls at floors wait? The logic with passengers >0 and dests outranks everything, but should eventually. However crowd at 0 pressing up constantly plus upper-floor people pressing down. SCAN should alternate.\n\nLet's simulate logic alone with many random calls to see throughput. But the elevator serves one direction fully then reverses, so if there's a continuous stream of up calls from 0 and upper floors, down calls wait until no up work ahead. Since up calls at 0 are behind when car is going up; after reaching top, it reverses and should serve down calls at 4,2,1 before reaching 0. It does. But when it reaches floor4 going down, debug shows down call 4 present while car at 4 direction up with dest5. It will next go 5, reverse, then down4. So at most one extra trip.\n\nMaybe the bottleneck is the huge crowd at floor0: each trip up takes 4, then returns down. With 30 people, 8 trips; at 600x ~ maybe 0.4 real sec. Not 9 hours. Something else: agents waiting at floor0 might not be served because `isAcceptingAt` rejects them due direction mismatch when car opens at 0 while direction down and there are still down stops ahead? At floor0 there are no floors below, so `_hasStopsAhead(-1)` false -> accepts up callers. Good.\n\nBut wait: When car reaches floor0 going down, it clears downCalls at 0 (none) and because `!_hasStopsAhead(-1)` true, clears upCalls 0. Then direction remains -1. Waiting up callers check `isAcceptingAt(0,+1)`: direction -1, hasStopsAhead(-1) false -> true. They board. But only 4. Others wait; their WAIT_AT_PANEL re-presses up0 every frame. However car remains DOOR_OPEN with pending? After 4 board, no pending, door closes next tick. Up0 re-added by leftover waiters. At door close, `_pickNextTarget`: passengers 4 with destinations above -> choose dest. Good. So leaves. Fine.\n\nMaybe passengers' destinations are not above? Debug at floor4 up dest5 passengers1. There are also down calls. It seems serving.\n\nMaybe waiting counts include people at floor0 whose toFloor is 1,2 etc but they are behind a crowd and never reach panel? No, WAIT_AT_PANEL state means reached panel. They are at elevWait. They might be physically far? State set at start of WAIT before walking? No, plan walks to elevWait first. Fine.\n\nLet's check whether waiting agents ever get served over a short window. Track IDs waiting at two times. Could be same set stuck. Let's probe 10s apart and compare. Also check elevator calls. Use debug.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"At 12:52 many workers waiting to go down for lunch (dir -1) at floors 1,2,4, plus huge crowd at 0 waiting up. Elevator at floor4 direction UP with dest5, down calls 4,2,1. It is serving an up destination 5 before down calls. Then will reverse and serve down. But the crowd at 0 up call is also queued. This is expected queue but 29 waiting after 9 hours? The problem may be that elevator prioritizes current direction and keeps cycling up/down but capacity 4, with 60 people and lunch rush. But by 12:52 lunch starts 11:30; many waiting is plausible at 600x where door cycle maybe ~3 frames = 0.05s real; 29 people /4 =8 trips ~0.4s. Why 9 hours? Because many visitors keep going up/down for office activities, plus workers. Still queue should drain.\\n\\nMaybe there is a serious starvation due to hall call clearing rules. Notice up call 0 persists. Car at floor4 direction up, down calls 4,2,1. It will go to5 (dest), then reverse down, serve 4,2,1, then at 0? Up0 remains. It may serve down 1 then go to0? There is no down0 call; down call at floor1 cleared at open, but after floor1 it continues down to floor0 because direction down with no more down calls ahead? At door close at floor1, direction down, ahead none, reverse up, pool all: up0 and down? none -> target0 (up call) which is below current? Wait current1, direction reversed up (+1); pool all includes up0 at floor0 below, _nearest chooses 0, _setTarget floor0 (<current) sets direction -1 and MOVING down to0. Good. Then opens at0 (direction down), clears downCalls floor0 none, then if no stops ahead down (none), clears up0 because opposite. Good, up0 cleared! Then riders board? Direction is down but isAcceptingAt(0,+1): hasStopsAhead(down) false, so accepts up callers. They board, press upper. After close, pick passengers dest above -> up. Good. So up0 should clear at open. But debug shows