er car remains DOOR_OPEN with pending? After 4 board, no pending, door closes next tick. Up0 re-added by leftover waiters. At door close, `_pickNextTarget`: passengers 4 with destinations above -> choose dest. Good. So leaves. Fine.\\n\\nMaybe passengers' destinations are not above? Debug at floor4 up dest5 passengers1. There are also down calls. It seems serving.\\n\\nMaybe waiting counts include people at floor0 whose toFloor is 1,2 etc but they are behind a crowd and never reach panel? No, WAIT_AT_PANEL state means reached panel. They are at elevWait. They might be physically far? State set at start of WAIT before walking? No, plan walks to elevWait first. Fine.\\n\\nLet's check whether waiting agents ever get served over a short window. Track IDs waiting at two times. Could be same set stuck. Let's probe 10s apart and compare. Also check elevator calls. Use debug.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bca194cc2862f034","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cat > /tmp/office_stuck.js <<'EOF'\nconst http=require('http'),fs=require('fs'),path=require('path');\nconst {chromium}=require('playwright');\nconst dir=process.argv[2];\nconst server=http.createServer((req,res)=>{let u=decodeURIComponent((req.url||'/').split('?')[0]);let f=path.join(dir,u==='/'?'index.html':u);fs.readFile(f,(e,d)=>{if(e){res.writeHead(404);res.end();return}res.writeHead(200,{'Content-Type':path.extname(f)==='.html'?'text/html':'text/javascript'});res.end(d)})});\nserver.listen(0,'127.0.0.1',async()=>{\n const port=server.address().port; const browser=await chromium.launch({headless:true}); const page=await browser.newPage({viewport:{width:1200,height:900}});\n await page.goto(`http://127.0.0.1:${port}/index.html`,{waitUntil:'domcontentloaded'}); await page.waitForTimeout(500);\n await page.evaluate(()=>{const ins=Array.from(document.querySelectorAll(\"input[type='range']\")); ins[0].value=ins[0].max; ins[0].dispatchEvent(new Event('input',{bubbles:tr